hadiths[1002]{hadithnumber,text}:
"1003","(1003) Ibn Abi Zaydi told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abdul-Ala, on the authority of Ibn al-Hanafi, who said: It is nothing."
"1004","(1004) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hafsa, on the authority of Umm Atiyya, she said : We did not see triya as anything."
"1005","(1005) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: They did not see in yellow. And the turbidity is bad, meaning: after washing."
"1006","(1006) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the mirror you see yellowness after washing. He said: Perform ablution and pray."
"1007","(1007) Waki’ told us, on the authority of a partner, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata’; In the mirror you see yellowness after washing. He said: Perform ablution and pray."
"1008","(1008) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If she sees it after washing, then she should cleanse herself and perform ablution. And you pray."
"1009","(1009) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Do not wash until you see white purity. Like a story"
"1010","(1010) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I said to him: What is pure? He said: The dry white one, which does not contain any yellow or water. Holes: white."
"1011","(1011) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Sa`id, who said: I was sent to Raita, your master, Omar. Then the Messenger told me that she said: Omar used to say to the women: If one of you enters the carousel and comes out looking changed Do not pray until you do not see anything."
"1012","(1012) Muhammad ibn Bakr told us, on the authority of Yunus ibn Yazid al-Alayli, on the authority of al-Zuhri, he said: I asked him about what follows. Menstruation from bile and brownness? He said: It is menstruation, and you should abstain from praying until you purify yourself."
"1013","(1013) Abd al-A’la bin Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Fatima bint al-Mundhir, on the authority of Asma’ bint Abi Bakr, she said: We were in her room with her daughter’s daughters, and one of us was purifying herself, then praying, then she would lower herself. With the easy whistle, so we ask her? So you say: Aside from prayer as long as you see that, until you see nothing but pure white."
"1014","(1014) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, on the authority of his paternal aunt, on the authority of his son Zayd ibn Thabit said that she heard that women were calling with lamps in the middle of the night to look at the purity. She blames them and says: Women would not do this."
"1015","(1015) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Fatima, on the authority of Asmaa. She said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked. May God bless him and grant him peace, about menstrual blood being on the garment? He said: Pour it with water, wash it, and pray over it.\n(Bukhari 307, An-Nasa’i 285)"
"1016","(1016) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Adi bin Dinar; Umm Husayn asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, about menstrual blood that is on the garment? He said: Rub it with a rib, wash it with water and lotus leaves, and pray over it. (Ahmad 355, Ibn Majah 628)"
"1017","(1017) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Salamah; That a woman asked her about a menstruating woman wearing a garment that she prays in? Umm Salama said: If there is blood on it, she should wash the place of the blood, otherwise she should pray on it."
"1018","(1018) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’; The wives of Abdullah bin Omar and the mothers of his children used to menstruate, so when they were pure they did not wash the clothes they were wearing. They wear clothes during their menstruation, and Ibn Umar used to say: If you see blood, wash it with it."
"1019","(1019) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I asked him about menstrual blood. Is it in the dress? He said: Aisha said: It is enough for one of you to wash it with water."
"1020","(1020) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, he said: A woman should not wash her menstrual clothes if she wants, unless You see blood and wash it off."
"1021","(1021) Abu Amir Al-Aqdi told us, on the authority of Aflah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The menstruating woman used to wear her clothes, then She purifies herself, and if she does not see any in her garment, she sprinkles it, then prays in it."
"1022","(1022) Muhammad bin Bakr told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: A man said to Ataa: A menstruating woman is purified with blood on her clothes, not Is it enough for her to just wash off the blood and leave her clothes behind? He said: Yes."
"1023","(1023) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr; In the case of a menstruating woman, her dress is stained with her blood. He said: She washes it, then he smears its place with rose and saffron, or Amber"
"1024","(1024) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A woman should wash whatever gets on her clothes. Menstrual blood, not the douche of anything."
"1025","(1025) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of Muadh; That a woman asked Aisha about blood oozing into the garment? She said: Wash him with water, for water is pure."
"1026","(1026) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr bin Haram, who said: Jabir bin Zayd was asked about women. A menstruating woman gets blood on her dress, so she washes it and a trace of blood remains on it. Should you pray in it? He said: Yes."
"1027","(1027) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A woman prays in her clothes. The woman who menstruates, unless something happens to her, in which case she should wash the place of the blood."
"1028","(1028) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: I asked him about a woman who menstruates while wearing a garment? He said: There is no harm in it, unless you see something and wash it."
"1029","(1029) Sa’l bin Yusuf told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Al-Hikam; In the garment of a menstruating woman, he said: You wash where the blood is."
"1030","(1030) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When a menstruating woman purifies herself, her husband does not approach her until You wash yourself"
"1031","(1031) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, about a similar story."
"1032","(1032) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’ and Tawoos, who said: If the woman is cleansed of blood and the lustful man wants to He comes to her, let him command her to perform ablution, then let him pour some of her semen if he wishes."
"1033","(1033) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Al Aswad, on the authority of Mujahid; In a menstruating woman, the bleeding stops. He said: He should not have intercourse with her until it is permissible for her to pray."
"1034","(1034) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If the blood stops and her husband becomes estrus, he is afraid of it. On himself, let him order her to wash her private parts, then he may wash her genitals if he wishes."
"1035","(1035) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He disliked it for a man to have intercourse with his wife when she had been cleansed, before she had washed herself."
"1036","(1036) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Malik ibn Anas, on the authority of Abu Salama and Sulayman ibn Yasar, who said: No. Her husband comes to her until she bathes."
"1037","(1037) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, that he used to say: A man should not intercourse with a woman when she is pure. From menstruation until you bathe."
"1038","(1038) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Munib, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: If the blood stops from her, then he should not come to her. Until she is cleansed, then when she is cleansed, let him come to her as God commanded him."
"1039","(1039) Yahya bin Zakariya bin Abi Zayed told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a menstruating woman purifies herself She did not find water, so she performed tayammum, and her husband came to her."
"1040","(1040) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a woman is menstruating and sees the ritual purity while traveling, She performed tayammum on the earth to purify it, then he removed from it if he wished."
"1041","Al-Hasan bin Saeed told us, he said: Abu Abdul Rahman Buqi bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Abu Bakr Abdullah bin Muhammad told us Ibn Abi Shaybah said:\n(1041) Abu Bakr bin Ayash narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mu’awiyah bin Qurayh, who said: He came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. A group of Banu Qushayr greeted him and said: We are cut off from water, and our family is with us, and there is no water with us except to heal us. He said: Yes, even if that was a year or two."
"1042","(1042) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Ibn Abbas was on a journey with people. Among the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was Ammar bin Yasser, and they used to lead him in front of him and he would lead them in prayer. Because of his closeness to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, he led them in prayer one day, then he turned to them and laughed. So he told them that he had prayed with one of his Roman neighbours, and he prayed with them while he was on his side, performing tayammum."
"1043","(1043) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zaid, he was asked about a man who is single and has his family with him? He said: He comes to his family and performs tayammum."
"1044","(1044) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Abu Al-Awwam, who said: I was sitting with Ibn Omar, and he came A Bedouin, and he said to him: We are isolated from water among our livestock, so one of us needs to harm his family. He said: Either Ibn Omar did not do that, but as for you, if you find water, take a bath."
"1045","(1045) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abu Abdullah al-Mawsili, who said: It was Ibn Awf and Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar were on a journey and could not find water, so Ibn Abbas fell, and they blamed him for that."
"1046","(1046) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan; They did not see any harm if a man was on a journey and did not have water with him, for him to get sick from his family, then He becomes an orphan."
"1047","(1047) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: If a man is on a journey, There are two or three nights between him and the water, so there is no harm in him interfering with one of his family, then performing tayammum."
"1048","(1048) Hafs told us, on the authority of a sheikh, who said: Salem used to have intercourse without water and perform tayammum when the water was solid."
"1049","(1049) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If he was in a deserted land, then he struck it. He is lustful and fears for himself, and his wife is with him, so he may have intercourse with her if he wishes."
"1050","(1050) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’; Abu Dharr was on a journey, so he had intercourse with his family, but he had no water."
"1051","(1051) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah; He hated to have intercourse when he could not find water."
"1052","(1052) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: We were with Ibn Abbas on a journey, and a female servant was with him. So he fell behind, and he took some of it. Then he caught up with us and said: Do you have any water? We said: No. He said: As for me, I knew that, so he performed tayammum."
"1053","(1053) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: When one of you gets up during the night, he should not dip his hand into a vessel until he has washed it three times. For he does not know where his hand has spent the night. (Muslim 233. Abu Dawud 104)"
"1054","(1054) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: When one of you gets up from his sleep, let him empty his vessel three times. For he does not know where his hand has spent the night. (Muslim 233. Tirmidhi 24)"
"1055","(1055) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: When one of you gets up during the night, he should not put his hand into the vessel until he has washed it. (Ahmad 5071 Muslim 233)"
"1056","(1056) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man wakes up from his sleep, he should not put his hand into it. The vessel until he washes it."
"1057","(1057) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: The sleeping person and the one who is awake are equal, if he is obliged to perform ablution. He should not put his hand into the vessel until he has washed it."
"1058","(1058) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The companions of Abdullah, when a hadith was mentioned to them, Abu Hurairah They said: How does Abu Hurairah make with the clay in Medina?"
"1059","(1059) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ubaidah; He used to put his hand into the vessel when it came out of the outlet, before washing it."
"1060","(1060) Abd al-Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He used to come out of the toilet, then He puts his hand in the vessel before washing it."
"1061","(1061) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: I saw Ibrahim urinating, then he put his hand into the vessel before He washes her."
"1062","(1062) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Al-Mughiry, the thief, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about the man who dips his hands in water. His hand in the vessel, before he washed it? He said: No problem."
"1063","(1063) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mahdi ibn Maymun, on the authority of Ismail ibn Ibrahim, he said: I saw Salim go. He urinated, then put all his hands into the vessel before washing them."
"1064","(1064) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of al-Salt ibn Bahram, he said: I saw Ibrahim urinating, then he put his hand into it. In the vessel before he washed it, he said: I cleaned it, he said: Then he smiled and said: There is no man more severe in this than me, I have not Enter it except while it is pure."
"1065","(1065) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Bara’; He put his hand into the purifier before he washed it. Al-A'mash said: This is a letter I find good."
"1066","(1066) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, he said: Abu Ishaq told us, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, he said: He called for water and washed himself. He held out his hands three times, before putting them into the vessel, then he said: This is how I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He made"
"1067","(1067) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: If a man urinates or urinates, he should not enter it. His hand is in the vessel until he washes it."
"1068","(1068) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Salam bin Abi Dhayal, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If you want to perform ablution, then do not Dip your hands in the vessel until you purify them."
"1069","(1069) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Hayya, who said: I saw Ali performing ablution and purifying himself. He sufficed him, then washed his face and arms, then said: I only wanted to show you the purification of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace."
"1070","(1070) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was said: Wash the hair and cleanse the skin, in Impurity"
"1071","(1071) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Under every hair is a graveyard, so wet the hair and cleanse it. Good news"
"1072","(1072) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’abi, on the authority of Amr ibn Murra, on the authority of Abu al-Bakhtari, who said: Hudhayfy came out, and he He combed his hair and said: “Underneath all of your hair is something that water cannot touch.” So they treated her well, so I treated my head as it was. You see?"
"1073","(1073) Aswad bin Amir told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever leaves a place of hair on his body from his side and does not wash it, do the same. Such and such from the Fire. Ali said: Then I became hostile to my hair. He said: He used to cut his hair. (Ahmad 1/101, Abu Dawud 253)"
"1074","(1074) Abu Dawud narrated to us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Under every hair of your body, he said: And Abu Hurairah said: As for me, I am the most beautiful of hair and the purest of human beings. (Abu Dawud 252. Tirmidhi 106)"
"1075","(1075) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fudayl bin Ghazwan, on the authority of Nafi’; When Ibn Umar took a bath after ritual impurity, he would put water in his eyes and put his hand in his navel."
"1076","(1076) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: If he becomes junub The man had wounds and smallpox, so he feared for himself if he bathed. He said: He should perform tayammum in the desert."
"1077","(1077) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim. And on the authority of Al-Hasan and Al-Shaabi; They said about the one who has a wound, the one that is harvested, and the one that is twisted: he should perform tayammum."
"1078","(1078) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He used to say about the one with sores and the one who fears for Himself: to perform tayammum."
"1079","(1079) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’. And about the ruling, about the divider, they said: The man has ulcers, wounds, and smallpox. He cannot absorb water as he performs tayammum."
"1080","(1080) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ezra, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr; Concerning a man who has wounds, ulcers, or illness, and the impurity afflicts him, so washing him is difficult for him. He said: He becomes an orphan."
"1081","(1081) Ibn Ghaniyya told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hikam; Concerning a sick person who is in a state of junubah and there is fear for him if he performs ghusl. He said: He performs tayammum."
"1082","(1082) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Mujahid, that he said in Al-Majdur and its likes: So Fear for them, so they are in the same position as a traveler, performing tayammum."
"1083","(1083) Abdul Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abi Farwa, on the authority of Ata’; That a man had a wet dream during the time of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, while he was braided, so they washed him, and he died, and that was conveyed to the Prophet. May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, and he said: They lost him, God lost them. They killed him, God killed them. (Abu Dawud 340)"
"1084","(1084) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salama, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to recite the Qur’an to us in every situation, except during ritual impurity. (Abu Dawud 232. Tirmidhi 146. Ahmad 1/134)"
"1085","(1085) Hafs bin Ghayath and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salam, on the authority of Ali, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Like him"
"1086","(1086) Hafs and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Ubaydah, on the authority of Omar, who said: He who is in a state of junub is not recited. The Qur’an."
"1087","(1087) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Ibn Masoud was walking towards the Euphrates, and he was reciting to a man, then Ibn Masoud urinated, so the man stopped him and said: Ibn Masoud: What's wrong with you? He said: You have urinated. Ibn Masoud said: I am not in a state of sexual impurity."
"1088","(1088) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Al-Muhajir, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, he said: It is not recited. The side"
"1089","(1089) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: The junub person should not recite the Qur’an."
"1090","(1090) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amer, who said: A woman in a state of impurity or a menstruating woman does not recite the Qur’an."
"1091","(1091) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Sha’bi, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: The impure or menstruating woman should not recite the Qur’an."
"1092","(1092) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Aamir bin Al-Samit, on the authority of Abu Al-Gharaif, on the authority of Ali, who said: It is not recited, not even a letter, meaning: The side"
"1093","(1093) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: A junub person should not recite the Qur’an, and he said: If he recites, he prays."
"1094","(1094) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ja`far, on the authority of his father; He saw no harm in a junub or menstruating woman reciting anything from the Qur’an."
"1095","(1095) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah; He did not see any harm in a person who is in a state of ritual impurity reciting the verse and two verses."
"1096","(1096) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’. On the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Saeed bin Jubayr; In menstruating women and in a state of impurity, they begin the beginning of the verse, but do not complete the last of it."
"1097","(1097) Sharik told us, on the authority of Aamir bin Al-Samat, on the authority of Abu Al-Gharaif, on the authority of Ali, who said: It is not read, not even a letter."
"1098","(1098) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Omar bin Abdullah, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr: A menstruating woman should recite And the side? He said: The verse and the two verses."
"1099","(1099) Ubayd Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Omar bin Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Maqil, similar to that."
"1100","(1100) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, who said: The one who is in a state of ritual impurity recites the Qur’an. He said: So I mentioned it to Abraham, and he thought about it."
"1101","(1101) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah, who said: A menstruating woman should not recite the Qur’an."
"1102","(1102) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: A menstruating woman should not recite the Qur’an."
"1103","(1103) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: You recite from what is less than the verses, but you do not recite A complete verse"
"1104","(1104) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Omar, who said: A menstruating woman should not recite the Qur’an."
"1105","(1105) Sharik told us, on the authority of Firas, on the authority of Amer; Do not read the Qur’an."
"1106","(1106) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Yazid, he said: We were with Salman. In need, he went and fulfilled his need and then came back, so we said to him: Perform ablution, O Abu Abdullah, perhaps we will ask you about a verse. From the Qur’an? He said: He said: So ask, for I will not touch it. None will touch it except the cleansed. He said: So we asked him, and he recited to us before he He performs ablution."
"1107","(1107) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Yazid bin Muawiyah, on the authority of Alqamiya and Al-Aswad; Salman recited to them after the event."
"1108","(1108) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, And Ibn Umar said: They used to recite parts of the Qur’an after they had gone out of the toilet, before they performed ablution."
"1109","(1109) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin al-Musayyab; That Abu Hurairah used to leave the exit and then recite the surah."
"1110","(1110) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Muhammad; Omar fulfilled his need, then he began to recite, and Abu Maryam said to him: If only you performed ablution, O Commander of the Faithful. So Omar said to him : Am I a Muslim? Did that give you a fatwa?!"
"1111","(1111) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah. On the authority of Abu Maryam, on the authority of Omar, in the same way."
"1112","(1112) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, who said: Omar came out of the privacy and recited a verse from a book. God, so it was said to him: Do you recite when you have narrated? He said: Should a Muslim person recite that?"
"1113","(1113) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Abdullah bin Salamah, on the authority of Ali, who said: The Messenger of God May God’s prayers and peace be upon him, we recite the Qur’an in every situation, as long as it is not in a state of ritual junub."
"1114","(1114) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Nafi’ ibn Jubayr; He saw no harm in reciting the Qur’an other than purity."
"1115","(1115) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Hamid, on the authority of Abu Jafar, he said: Ali bin Hussein used to recite The Qur’an after the event."
"1116","(1116) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; What about a man who sheds water and recites the Qur’an? He said: It is more beloved to me to be in a pure state, unless he is reciting the end of the verse, or something."
"1117","(1117) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Perhaps I came down while I was on a journey. To relieve myself of defecation and urine, I will not join my friends until I read part of the Qur’an before I perform ablution."
"1118","(1118) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: I was reading from the Qur’an, and he came out. I am alone, and I learned some verses, so he reminded me of them."
"1119","(1119) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Read the Qur’an in every circumstance. Unless you are on the side."
"1120","(1120) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; He used to recite after the hadith."
"1121","(1121) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It used to be said: Read the Qur’an in every circumstance. Unless you are on the side."
"1122","(1122) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah; There was a man with him, and he urinated and then came, and Ibn Masoud said to him: Read it."
"1123","(1123) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr; Ibn Abbas and Ibn Umar used to recite the Qur’an after they left the state of Hadath, before they performed ablution."
"1124","(1124) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Ali, who said: If a man commits impurity in a land, there is water with him. If someone is easy going, let him prefer water, and let him perform tayammum in the desert."
"1125","(1125) Abu Bakr ibn Ayyash told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’ and Tawoos who said: If you are on a journey and you do not have water with you If only he could walk, perform tayammum, and keep water ahead of him."
"1126","(1126) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: If you are traveling while you are in a state of ritual impurity, or you are not performing ablution, and you are afraid that if you perform ablution you will die of thirst. So do not perform ablution and keep it for yourself."
"1127","(1127) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, the same."
"1128","(1128) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid; When Omar urinated, he would perform tayammum, saying: I will perform tayammum until it is permissible for me to praise Allah."
"1129","(1129) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Whenever Ibn Umar urinated and wanted to eat, he performed ablution, but did not He washes his feet."
"1130","(1130) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, who said: We used to be with Abraham and he would go and urinate. Then he comes and touches the water and says: They used to like to touch the water when they urinated."
"1131","(1131) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Misra, on the authority of Tawus, who both said: I saw Ibn Umar and Ibn Abbas: When they come out of the toilet, they face each other, so they wash their faces and hands."
"1132","(1132) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It has reached me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not He enters the bathroom unless he performs ablution or touches water."
"1133","(1133) Ibn Al-Mubarak told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: Urwa told me, on the authority of his father; Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq said, while he was addressing the people: O community of Muslims, be ashamed before God, for by Him who is my soul. In his hand, when I go to the toilet, I remain in space, covering my head out of shame before my Lord."
"1134","(1134) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of Thabit, on the authority of Anas, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: I wash myself in a dark house, so I bow my back when I take my garment out of respect from my Lord."
"1135","(1135) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja’far Al-Khutami, on the authority of Amara bin Khuzaymah, and Al-Harith bin Fudail, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Qarad, who said: I performed Hajj with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He said: So he went to fulfill his need. So he went away.\n(Ahmad 3/443, Ibn Majah 334)"
"1136","(1136) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Musa bin Abdullah bin Yazid, on the authority of a servant of Aisha On the authority of Aisha, she said: She never saw or saw the private parts of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace.\n(Ahmad 6/63, Tirmidhi 359)"
"1137","(1137) Abd Allah bin Sulayman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amer, he said: My father saw me. And a man, while we were bathing, he poured water on me and I poured water on him. He said: He shouted at us and said: Did the man see the private parts of the man?! By God, I see you as a successor."
"1138","(1138) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, who said: Umar said: A man should not see another man’s private parts, or He said: A man should not look at a man's private parts."
"1139","(1139) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Al-Ghaz, on the authority of Ubadah bin Nasi, on the authority of Qays bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Salman, who said: Because I die and then I am raised, then I die and then I am raised, then I die and then I am raised, is more beloved to me than seeing a man’s private parts, or him seeing his semen."
"1140","(1140) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Ubadah ibn Nasi, on the authority of Abu Musa, he said: Because I die and then I am more beloved to me than having my private parts seen."
"1141","(1141) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, who said: My father ordered me when I entered the toilet to cover my head. I said: Why? Did he order you to do that? He said: I don't know."
"1142","(1142) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of al-Dahhak ibn Uthman, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abu Saeed Al-Khudri, on the authority of his father, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: A man should not look at his private parts. The man, nor the woman, except the private parts of the woman. (Abu Dawud 4014. An-Nasa’i 9229)q"
"1143","(1143) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’bi, he said: I was with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and he said: O Mughirah, take the medicine. He said: So I took it, then I went out with him, and the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, set off until he disappeared and fulfilled his need. (Bukhari 363. An-Nasa’i 9663)"
"1144","(1144) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, saying: Ismail ibn Abdul-Malik informed me, on the authority of Abu al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, He said: I went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, but the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not come. Stool until it disappears and is not visible. (Abu Dawud 2. Ibn Majah 335)"
"1145","(1145) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, he said: Abdullah bin Omar said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was When a pilgrim wanted to come, he would stand out so that no one could see him, and he would not lift his garment until he was close to the ground. (Tirmidhi 14)"
"1146","(1146) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: Abu Musa said: I did not set my cross in I have been washed since I converted to Islam."
"1147","(1147) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I said to Ibrahim: Should I wash myself with the pigeon water? He said: If you take it from his stone, that will be sufficient for you."
"1148","(1148) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: If I had washed myself with it, I would not have washed myself with it."
"1149","(1149) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: I told him: Do the Magians and the Junub enter the bathroom? He said: The water is pure, nothing can make it impure."
"1150","(1150) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: Bath water is sufficient for impurity."
"1151","(1151) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He was entering it, and when he was leaving, he would face the gutter, wash himself, then go out."
"1152","(1152) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi; He used to enter and bathe in it and say: If I had bathed in it, I would not have entered it."
"1153","(1153) Ishaq bin Mansour told us, he said: Huraim told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: He and the lions were washed with bath water, and they were not boiled during washing."
"1154","(1154) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of Al-Hazzaz, on the authority of Ibn Abza, who said: He only made The bathroom is to be purified with it, and not to be purified from it."
"1155","(1155) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ziyad bin Fayyad, on the authority of Ibn Abzi, similar to this."
"1156","(1156) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ubaid Al-Bahrani, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about Bath water? He said: Water does not run away."
"1157","(1157) Ubaidah bin Hamid narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Farwa Al-Hamdani, on the authority of Al-Shu’abi, he said: I asked him: Should I wash myself with water? Bath water if you are in the state of Janub? He said: Yes, then I prepared him to perform the ablution. He said: So I said to him: Do you perform ablution when you come out of it? He said: Why did I let him in then?"
"1158","(1158) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Raja’i, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated to wash himself with bath water."
"1159","(1159) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Sayyar, who said: I saw Al-Sha’abi come out of the bathroom and start wading through the water, but he did not He washed his feet. He said: So I told him about that? He said: I am a man to be looked at."
"1160","(1160) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Washing with bath water."
"1161","(1161) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr; He was taking a bath in the bathroom."
"1162","(1162) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of a man from the Ansar On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Two waters are not sufficient: sea water and pigeon water."
"1163","(1163) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’ah ibn Kulthum, who said: I heard Al-Hasan say: When you leave the bathroom, take a bath."
"1164","(1164) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: There is no harm in the gnawing of an animal."
"1165","(1165) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in donkey saliva."
"1166","(1166) Ishaq bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Hammad, who said: Beware of what flows from the mouth of an animal."
"1167","(1167) Ibn Aliyah told us, he said: I asked Yunus about donkey sweat and its saliva getting on clothes? He said: I don't know of any harm in him unless he is filthy by them."
"1168","(1168) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, he said: I asked Ibrahim about a dog that stained my dress? He said: It stained you. With something? I said: No, and he said: It will not harm you."
"1169","(1169) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ubaidah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm in donkey saliva."
"1170","(1170) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin: They were a threat to entering The bathroom"
"1171","(1171) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Ibn Omar, he said: Do not enter the bathroom, for Of the bliss they have created."
"1172","(1172) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Zar’i, who said: Ali said: An evil house is the dove."
"1173","(1173) Hushaym told us, saying: Dawud bin Amr told us, on the authority of Atiyya bin Qais, on the authority of Abu Darda’; He was entering the bathroom. He said: And he used to say: What a beautiful house the bathroom is, removing the polish, meaning: the dirt. And he mentions the Fire."
"1174","(1174) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; He entered the bathroom."
"1175","(1175) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He entered the bathroom of Al-Juhfa."
"1176","(1176) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Amara, on the authority of Abu Zur’a, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: What an excellent house is the bathroom. It removes the dirt, and reminds of the Fire."
"1177","(1177) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Uthman ibn Qais, who said: I went out with Jarir on a Friday to go to his bath. With reason."
"1178","(1178) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of his father, who said: Ali Al-Hussein bin Ali was mine. A debt, so I came to him to pay it off, and I found him coming out of the bathroom with henna on his nails, and his female slave had an itch. On him is the trace of henna in a bottle."
"1179","(1179) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Atiyya, on the authority of Ibn Omar, who said: What an excellent house is the bathroom, it eliminates tuberculosis. And he mentions the Fire."
"1180","(1180) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: I passed to the bathroom and Abu Sadiq saw me and said: With you. Izar, for Ali used to say: Whoever exposes his private parts, the king will turn away from him."
"1181","(1181) Hushaym narrated to us, saying: Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders; Omar bin Al-Khattab wrote that no one should enter the bathroom except with an apron."
"1182","(1182) Ziyad bin Al-Rabi’ told us, on the authority of Ghalib Al-Qattan; Omar bin Abdul Aziz wrote to his governor in Basra, and then: It is from you that they enter the bathroom except With an apron."
"1183","(1183) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Daoud Al-Dhabi, on the authority of Muslim Al-Batin, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, He said: It is forbidden for him to enter the bathroom without a garment."
"1184","(1184) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa narrated to us, on the authority of Ziyad ibn Abd al-Rahman, who said: I saw Abu Ja`far entering the bathroom wearing a garment. Up to the knees, and there are people without clothes."
"1185","(1185) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Salama and Ash’ath, on the authority of Muhammad; He hated to enter the bathroom without a garment, and he hated to enter it with a garment, and others were not wearing a garment. He says: He sees her private parts."
"1186","(1186) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Omar wrote to the commanders of the soldiers: No. No man enters the bathroom unless he is wearing an apron, and no woman unless he is sick."
"1187","(1187) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Amr ibn Maimun, who said: If one of you enters the bathroom, or Euphrates, let him cover himself and wear clothes."
"1188","(1188) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, who said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz beating the owner of the bathroom. And whoever enters it without a garment."
"1189","(1189) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, who said: I saw Omar bin Abdul Aziz being flogged with a handkerchief. In the bathroom, and the owner of the bathroom is punished."
"1190","(1190) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Abdullah bin Shaddad told us, on the authority of Abu Uthrah, and he had The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, learned, on the authority of Aisha, that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade men and women from Bathrooms, except for a sick person or postpartum woman. (Abu Dawud 4005. Tirmidhi 2802)"
"1191","(1191) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who raised it; He said: Whoever of you enters it, let him cover himself."
"1192","(1192) Malik bin Ismail narrated to us, on the authority of Kamil, on the authority of Habib, who said: A peacock, a peacock, and a mujahid entered the pigeons. So they neglected it."
"1193","(1193) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May the peace and blessings of God be upon him, Abu Bakr, and Omar, they will not be neglected."
"1194","(1194) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abdullah bin Shaddad, who said: When she saw him, she thought he was deep in darkness. And she uncovered her legs, and behold, there was a woman with hairs, he said: Then Solomon said: What does this mean? They said: The light. He said: So you were made the light on that day."
"1195","(1195) Azhar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Al-Hasan was a virtuous man, and he did not show off."
"1196","(1196) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Omar bin Hamza; Indeed, Salim recited one time and recited another time."
"1197","(1197) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd: He was negligent in the ten days."
"1198","(1198) Hushaym and Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith Abi Al-Mushrifi, on the authority of Abi Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It was When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, neglected his guardian, she suffered from him. (Ibn Majah 3752)"
"1199","(1199) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Qays al-Asadi, on the authority of Ali ibn Abi Aisha, who said: Umar was a man with a white hair. He was shaving his hair, and I mentioned the light to him, and he said: The light is part of bliss."
"1200","(1200) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of Imran bin Husayn said: Whoever urinates in his bath has not purified himself."
"1201","(1201) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Aisha, who said: God has not purified a man who urinates in his bath, Ataa said: If it is flowing, then there is no problem."
"1202","(1202) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan and Misra: They disliked that a man urinate in The one who has been bathed."
"1203","(1203) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, who said: Al-Hassan hated for a man to urinate in his bath."
"1204","(1204) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: Al-Hasan used to hate urinating in his bathtub. He said: Bakr bin Abdullah said: He used to say: He arouses obsession."
"1205","(1205) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh bin Abi Rashid, who said: I said to Anas’ concubine: Anas was urinating. Is there a bather in it? She said: No, I used to put a bowl for him and he would urinate in it."
"1206","(1206) Omar told us, on the authority of Isa, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah; He hated urinating in the bath."
"1207","(1207) Omar told us, on the authority of Aflah, he said: I saw Al-Qasim urinating in his bathtub."
"1208","(1208) Shabab told us, he said: Shu’bah told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Uqba bin Subhan, he said: I heard Abdullah bin A foolish adulterer says: Urine in the bathing person removes obsession from him."
"1209","(1209) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of someone who heard Anas ibn Malik say: He only disliked urinating in the bath, out of fear. The lam"
"1210","(1210) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, on the authority of Ata’; He saw no harm in a man wearing a ring, entering the toilet with it, having intercourse with it, and having a name on it. God"
"1211","(1211) Abd al-Rahman ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a, on the authority of Salamah ibn Wahram, on the authority of Ikrimah, he said: Ibn When Abbas enters the private room, he gives me his ring."
"1212","(1212) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin; About a man entering the exit with a ring in his hand with the name of God on it. He said: There is no harm in it."
"1213","(1213) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Rawwad, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: He used to say: If a man enters the private room, and A ring on it is the remembrance of God Almighty. He made the ring from what is next to the inside of his hand, then he tied it with his finger."
"1214","(1214) Abu Muawiyah told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Al-Manyal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Whenever Suleiman bin Dawud entered the toilet, he would take off his ring and give it to his wife."
"1215","(1215) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Ibrahim bin Nafi’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of Mujahid; It was disliked for man to enter the shroud, and upon it was a seal bearing the name of God."
"1216","(1216) Ibn Aliyah told us, he said: I asked Ibn Abi Najih; About the man entering the toilet carrying white dirhams? He said: He was Mujahid and hated him."
"1217","(1217) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He saw no harm in a man entering the toilet with him. White dirhams. He said: Al-Qasim bin Muhammad disliked them, and he did not see any harm in buying or selling them."
"1218","(1218) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of his father, who said: Whenever Muhammad ibn Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd entered the private room with him Dirhams, He gave them to a person who held them until he performed ablution."
"1219","(1219) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: I asked him about a man who urinated while carrying white coins? He said: People have no need to protect their money."
"1220","(1220) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: I prefer to have it between my skin, or my palm, And between them is a garment."
"1221","(1221) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim; He used to hate touching white dirhams without performing ablution."
"1222","(1222) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Qasim; He saw no harm in touching white dirhams without performing ablution."
"1223","(1223) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Haytham, he said: I asked Ibrahim about the man White dirhams without ablution? He thought that"
"1224","(1224) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm in him touching her otherwise than Ablution"
"1225","(1225) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Rabi’, who said: Ibn Sirin disliked it."
"1226","(1226) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer and Salem, who said: A man should not touch dirhams. In it is the Book of God, and it is a junub. He said: Ata’ and Al-Qasim said: He touches it if it is wrapped in a rag."
"1227","(1227) Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He said: He hates that God be mentioned while he is sitting on his privates, and a man is having intercourse with his wife, because He is the Possessor of Majesty. He is exalted. About that"
"1228","(1228) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Ata’, who said: The angels do not bear witness to your companions."
"1229","(1229) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Sayyar, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, who said: Two of which God does not remember the servant: When a man comes to his family, he begins by calling God, and if he is alone, he begins by calling God."
"1230","(1230) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Four no. They recite the Qur’an: when private, and during intercourse, and in a state of sexual impurity, and in a menstruating woman, except for a woman in sexual impurity and a menstruating woman, for they recite the Qur’an Verses and the like."
"1231","(1231) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Abi Marwan Al-Aslami, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ka’b, He said: Moses, peace be upon him, said: Which Lord are you near, so I will speak to you, or far away, so I will call you? He said: O Moses, I am sitting with the one who mentioned me. He said: O Lord, we are always in a state to glorify you, or to glorify you. Do we mention you to her? He said: What is it? He said: impurity and defecation. He said: O Moses, remember Me in every state."
"1232","(1232) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; Concerning a man sneezing in the open air, he said: Praise be to God."
"1233","(1233) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Praise be to God, for He is ascending."
"1234","(1234) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He praises God within himself."
"1235","(1235) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; He was asked about a man sneezing in the open? He said: I do not know of any harm in mentioning Allah."
"1236","(1236) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Abu Ishaq; Concerning a man sneezing in the open, he said: Abu Misra said: I do not like to remember God except in a good place. He said: Mansour said: Ibrahim said: Praise be to God."
"1237","(1237) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Qaz’a bin Suwayd told us, he said: I asked Ibn Abi Malika about the man. He sneezes while in the open air? He said: Thank God."
"1238","(1238) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, and Nafi’, who said: They saw no harm in the urine of a camel. He said: Did it happen to me? He saw no harm in it."
"1239","(1239) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, on the authority of Ata’; He was asked about camel urine getting on a man’s clothes? He said: What do you have to do if it happens to you? Hammad said: I wash myself with all my urine."
"1240","(1240) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, who said: Al-Hakam bin Safwan asked Ibrahim about Paul Does a camel stain a man’s clothing? He said: There is no problem with it. Isn’t it something he can drink and be treated with?"
"1241","(1241) Hafs told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If he regurgitates, there is no harm in his urine."
"1242","(1242) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: It was permitted regarding the urine of pregnant women."
"1243","(1243) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about the urine of the sheep? He said: Hammad: He should be washed, and the arbiter said: No."
"1244","(1244) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He was of the opinion that urine should be washed completely."
"1245","(1245) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to wash away all of the urine, and he used to cleanse the urine of corseted women."
"1246","(1246) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Ali bin Hakim, on the authority of Nafi’, and Abd al-Rahman bin Al-Qasim is that they said: Wash away any of the urine of animals that has come upon you."
"1247","(1247) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Misra, a servant of Al-Hayy, who said: I asked Al-Sha’abi about the urine of the goat? He said: Do not wash it."
"1248","(1248) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Ata, who said: Whatever the flesh of which is eaten, there is no problem. With his urine"
"1249","(1249) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Ammar bin Abi Hafsiya, who said: I heard Abu Majliz say: I said: By Ibn Omar: I sent my camel to urinate, and his urine hit me. He said: Wash him. I said: He was only excreted by such-and-such, meaning: He said: Wash him."
"1250","(1250) Khalid bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Issa bin Kathir, on the authority of Maymun bin Mihran, who said: The urine of animals and humans Either way"
"1251","(1251) Ibn Fadil narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Shubarmah, who said: I was with Al-Sha’bi in the market, and a mule urinated, so I stepped away from it. He said: What is wrong with you if it happens to you?"
"1252","(1252) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Jahadi, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm in sprinkling animal urine."
"1253","(1253) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of `Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Ibrahim, and Jabir, on the authority of Amir, the same."
"1254","(1254) Asbat bin Muhammad told us, on the authority of Mutarrif, on the authority of Al-Hakam, who said: If an animal’s urine spreads on you and you see its traces So wash it, and if you do not see any traces of it, leave it."
"1255","(1255) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to make a concession in the urine of bats."
"1256","(1256) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that he used to say: Whatever comes out of the wound is In the same way as blood, and in it is ablution."
"1257","(1257) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, he said: I heard him say: Pus and blood are the same."
"1258","(1258) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Pus and pus do not contain ablution."
"1259","(1259) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz; He did not see anything in the pus. He said: God only mentioned the blood."
"1260","(1260) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim. And on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad, they said: Whatever comes out of a blister is of the same quality as blood."
"1261","(1261) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: We were sitting with Abdullah when something happened to him. A bird, and he said to it: This is how it is with his hand. He shook it off."
"1262","(1262) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: I saw him, and a Meccan bird was thrown at him. So he started wiping it with his hand."
"1263","(1263) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: A mother fell on Al-Hasan and it splashed on him, and some of them said to him: People: Shall we bring you water for you to wash yourself with? He said: No, and started wiping it off."
"1264","(1264) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Ashhab al-Saadi, who said: I saw Yazid bin Abdullah bin al-Shakhir, the father of Al-Ala’ A bird flew over him while he was praying, so he wiped it off and then continued his prayer."
"1265","(1265) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hanzala, who said: I saw Salim and a bird had flown over him, so he wiped him and said: There is no harm in him."
"1266","(1266) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about bird droppings? They said: There is no harm in it."
"1267","(1267) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi Dhiyal, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who prayed, and when he finished his prayer, he saw a speck of chicken on his garment, so he said: It is a bird."
"1268","(1268) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ghaylan, on the authority of Hammad; He hated chicken droppings."
"1269","(1269) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwa; He used to prefer not to sleep except in a state of purity."
"1270","(1270) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He used to prefer not to sleep except in a state of purity."
"1271","(1271) Muhammad bin Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Whoever spends the night in a state of ritual purity with a penis, it will be upon him. his bed, prostrating to him until he gets up."
"1272","(1272) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Who among you is able to spend the night in a state of ritual purity, while maintaining his dhikr? , asking forgiveness for his sins, for we have learned that souls are resurrected for what they captured. (Bukhari 1245. Muslim 93)"
"1273","(1273) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Abu Salih al-Hanafi, who said: If a man goes to bed, The angel has anointed him pure. (Tirmidhi 3526)"
"1274","(1274) Ibn Ali told us, on the authority of Zaidah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Shahr, on the authority of Abu Imamah, who said: He who spends the night remembering is pure. Then he fell ill at night, and he did not ask God for anything he needed in this world or the hereafter, but God granted it to him."
"1275","(1275) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: It was narrated on the authority of Ibn Abbas; When he got up during the night, he would perform tayammum."
"1276","(1276) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: The Awwam told us, on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Amr bin Absa, he said: So The man went to bed clean, and remembered God until his eyes overwhelmed him, and the first thing he said when he woke up was: Glory be to You, there is no god but You, forgive me. He has shed his sins just as a snake sheds its skin."
"1277","(1277) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, who said: Ali was asked about a man who touched raw meat. So something happens to his hand? He said: No, he does not have to perform ablution if he touches it."
"1278","(1278) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: He does not have to perform ablution, except To wash his hands."
"1279","(1279) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Hilal, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: He performs ablution with raw meat."
"1280","(1280) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who touched raw meat, he said: There is no harm in it, but he does not have to perform ablution."
"1281","(1281) Muhammad bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If he had any trace of it on his hand. Let him wash his hands, otherwise he should not wash them."
"1282","(1282) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Ghalib, on the authority of Abu Ja’far. On the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ataa; Concerning a man who gets urine on his garment and does not know where it is. They said: He washes the entire garment."
"1283","(1283) Humayd narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: He washes the garment All of it"
"1284","(1284) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abu Bakr ibn Hafs, on the authority of Aisha bin Sa’d, on the authority of Aisha’s husband The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; About urine getting on the clothes. She said: Sprinkling it."
"1285","(1285) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a garment that gets stained with urine, but he does not know where it is? He said: When he regains consciousness, he should wash it completely."
"1286","(1286) Ghandar told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of Al-Hikam; About a man who got urine on his clothes and it was hidden on him. He said: He should sprinkle it. Shu`ba said: And Abdul Khaliq told me, on the authority of Hammad, that he said: He sprinkled it. I asked Ibn Shubarmah, and he said: Search that place and wash it."
"1287","(1287) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; In a woman who dyes her hands without performing ablution, then she attends the prayer. He said: She removes what is on her hands when She wanted to pray."
"1288","(1288) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: It was desirable for a woman to wear her hair dyed when She had her menstruation while she was menstruating, so if she had her menstruation while not menstruating, there is no problem, except if she fell asleep or had intercourse. She released him and performed ablution."
"1289","(1289) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Abu Sa’id, an infant who belonged to Aisha, who said: A woman asked Aisha, Mother of the Believers, should I pray in the oven? She said: I asked him and forced him."
"1290","(1290) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar ibn al-Fadl, on the authority of Hayya bint Abdullah, on the authority of Aisha, that she said: When praying, I used to do that, and I was the best of the maids, or sisters, as a hairdresser."
"1291","(1291) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Our women They dye the best dye, they dye it after dinner and take it off before dawn."
"1292","(1292) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya, that he used to command his women to get their hair dyed. The days of our menstruation."
"1293","(1293) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of one of them; She sent for Salem to ask him about the pigment and attend the prayer? He said: Take it off, perform ablution, and pray."
"1294","(1294) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, on the authority of someone who heard Aisha, she said: Because you two are cut off is more beloved to me. Than to wipe off the pigment."
"1295","(1295) Al-Muharbibi told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: It was desirable for a woman to dye her hair while she was menstruating."
"1296","(1296) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ubaid Allah, on the authority of Umm Qais bin Muhsin, she said: I entered with a son of mine upon the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He did not eat the food, so he urinated on him, so he called for water to sprinkle it with him.\n(Bukhari 223, Abu Dawud 377)"
"1297","(1297) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Qaboos ibn Al-Mukhariq, on the authority of Lubab ibn Al-Harith, she said: Al-Hussein bin Ali was in the lap of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. So I said: O Messenger of God, give me your garment and wear a garment. He changed it and said: It is sprinkled with male urine and washed with female urine. (Abu Dawud 378. Ibn Khuzaymah 282)"
"1298","(1298) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought to a baby boy. He urinated on him, so he ran water over him and did not wash him. (Muslim 102. Ibn Majah 523)"
"1299","(1299) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of his brother Isa, on the authority of his father Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of his grandfather, Abi Layla, who said: We were sitting with the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, when Al-Hussein bin Ali came. He crawled until he sat on his chest, then urinated on him. He said: So we hastened to take him, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: My son built, then he called for water and poured it on him. (Tahawi 94)"
"1300","(1300) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Ja’far, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, entered Peace be upon him, and he greeted Umm al-Fadl, and with her was Hussein, so she handed it to him. He urinated on his stomach or on his chest, and she wanted to You take it from him, and the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Do not insult my son, do not insult my son, for the boy’s urine It is filtered, or sprinkled, and washed with the urine of a slave girl."
"1301","(1301) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Harb ibn Abi Al-Aswad, he said: He said: Ali: The urine of a boy is to be sprinkled, and the urine of a girl is to be washed. (Abu Dawud 380)"
"1302","(1302) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Both of them should be sprinkled unless they are eaten. Food"
"1303","(1303) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Fadl ibn Dulham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, on the authority of his mother, on the authority of Umm Salama, who said: He is washed off with urine. The slave girl, and sprinkled with the boy’s urine."
"1304","(1304) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Watery urine of a boy is applied to him."
"1305","(1305) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ma’n, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If there is a taste, he should wash, and if there is no taste. Pour water on it."
"1306","(1306) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Waqid, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A man said to him: One of us carries a child and causes him Did he hurt him? He said: If it has a taste, wash it, and if it does not have a taste, pour water over it."
"1307","(1307) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: Water is poured over the boy’s urine."
"1308","(1308) Muhammad bin Bukair narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: As long as the boy does not eat the food, you wash your clothes. Also from his urine and weapons? He said: Sprinkle water on him, or pour water on him. I said: So the boy licks food such as ghee and honey before he eats, and is that food? He said: Sprinkle on him, or pour water on him."
"1309","(1309) Muhammad bin Bukair narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, who said: The Sunnah has passed that it is permissible to sprinkle the urine of someone He did not eat the food, and the Sunnah passed by washing away the urine of children who ate the food."
"1310","(1310) Hushaym told us, he said: Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: Someone who saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, told me. He greeted Paul while sitting, and he was so surprised that we thought his hip would give way."
"1311","(1311) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Hurr told me, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to Don't be surprised until he feels sorry for him."
"1312","(1312) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Zayd ibn Wahhab, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Husna, he said: He came out against us. The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, had a pomegranate in his hand. He said: So he placed it, then sat down and urinated on it, and said: Some of them said: Look at him, he urinates like a woman urinates. Then the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, heard him and said: Woe to you. I did not know what happened to the companion of the Children of Israel. When urine got on them, they used to scratch it with scissors. He forbade them and was tortured. His grave\n(Abu Dawud 23. Ibn Majah 346)"
"1313","(1313) Waki’ and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Tawus, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The Messenger passed by God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, mentioned two graves, and he said: They will be tormented, and they will not be tormented for a grave, but one of them He did not hide himself from his urine, but the other one used to gossip. (Bukhari 6052; Ibn Majah 347)"
"1314","(1314) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I heard Abu Wa’il narrating that Abu Musa used to stress Concerning urine, and he said: If the Children of Israel urinated on one of them, they would follow him with the muqaradin. (Bukhari 226. Muslim 228)"
"1315","(1315) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Salih, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet May God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He said: The torment of the grave is greater than urine. (Ahmad 2/388, Daraqutni 128)"
"1316","(1316) Ali told us, he said: Qadamah bin Abdullah Al-Amiri told us, he said: Jisri told me, she said: she told me. Aisha, she said: A Jewish woman came to me and said: The torment of the grave is due to urine. I said: I lied, she said: Yes, Indeed, it tears off the skin and clothing. She said: Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, went out to the prayer, and it had risen. Our voices, and he said: What is this? So I told him, and he said: You are right. (Ahmad 6/61, An-Nasa’i 9966)"
"1317","(1317) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Al-Aswad bin Shayban narrated to us, saying: Bahr bin Marar narrated to us, on the authority of his grandfather, Abu Bakra, He said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, passed by two graves and said: They will be tortured, but they will not be tortured for a major cause. As for one of them, he will be tortured for urination, and as for the other, for his absence. (Ahmad 39. Ibn Majah 349)"
"1318","(1318) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Al-A’mash narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to the tribes of a people and urinated on them while standing. (Bukhari 224, Muslim 228)"
"1319","(1319) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Zaid, who said: I saw Umar Bal standing."
"1320","(1320) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash and Husayn, on the authority of Abu Dhabyan, who said: I saw Ali standing."
"1321","(1321) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Qubaisah; He saw Zayd bin Thabit urinating standing up."
"1322","(1322) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Hammad bin Zaid narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah Al-Rumi, he said: I saw Ibn Umar urinating standing up."
"1323","(1323) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, who said: A man from Banu Sa’d, one of the maternal uncles of Al-Muharrar bin Abi, narrated to me. Huraira, he said: I saw Abu Huraira who urinated standing."
"1324","(1324) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abi Yahya, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul Rahman, he said: I saw Saeed bin Al-Musayyab urinated standing up, so I said: O Abu Muhammad, do you urinate standing up? Aren't you afraid that it will happen to you? He said to me: Don’t you urinate while standing? I said: No, I said: That is the medicine for you."
"1325","(1325) Marwan bin Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, who said: I saw Al-Sha’bi urinating while standing."
"1326","(1326) Muadh bin Muadh narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, he said: I saw Muhammad urinating while standing, and he did not see any harm in it."
"1327","(1327) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, who said: I saw my father urinating while standing."
"1328","(1328) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Tu’ma al-Jaafari, who said: I saw Zayd ibn al-Asam urinating standing up."
"1329","(1329) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Zakariya, on the authority of Abdul Aziz Abi Abdullah, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: What is the matter with the Messenger of God? God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was standing except once, in a dune, which pleased him."
"1330","(1330) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Fitr, who said: I saw the arbitrator urinating standing up."
"1331","(1331) Abu Asama and Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; That Saad bin Ubadah urinated while standing."
"1332","(1332) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam bin Shurayh bin Hani’, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Who told you? The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, urinated while standing, so do not believe him. I saw him urinate while sitting. (Ahmad 6/213 Ibn Rahwi 1570)"
"1333","(1333) Ibn Idris and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of Umar, he said: What I have been standing ever since I converted to Islam."
"1334","(1334) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated urinating while standing and drinking while standing."
"1335","(1335) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, who said: Abdullah said: It is unfair to He urinates standing up."
"1336","(1336) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Khams, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah, who said: It used to be said: It is impure to urinate standing up."
"1337","(1337) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Harith, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: It is rude for him to urinate standing up."
"1338","(1338) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I heard him say: Ibn Sirin would sometimes spit and say To the man: Look, has the saliva changed? If it has changed, then he spits out the second, and if it has changed in the third, it is as if he is performing ablution, and if it is not in The third one changed and did not see ablution."
"1339","(1339) Ibrahim bin Sadiqa told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who spat and saw blood in his sputum, he did not see anything in it that was not pure blood."
"1340","(1340) Hafs told us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not see anything in the jaundice except that it was dirty blood, meaning: in slugs."
"1341","(1341) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Sinan Al-Barjami, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; He spits on the man, and there is blood in his spit. He said: If the redness is predominant with the whiteness, he performs ablution, and if the whiteness is predominant The red one did not perform ablution."
"1342","(1342) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Abdullah ibn Abi Sara, who said: I saw a healthy man spitting out red blood, then He called for water and rinsed his mouth, but did not perform ablution and entered the mosque."
"1343","(1343) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ata’ bin Al-Sa’ib, who said: I saw Ibn Abi Awfa Bazaq while he was praying. Then he continued his prayer."
"1344","(1344) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad; Concerning a man who was performing ablution, and he saw bile in the sputum, and he said: It is nothing, unless it is liquid blood."
"1345","(1345) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Salim, and Al-Qasim; In Al-Saffarah in Al-Bazzaq, they said: Leave what confuses you for what does not confuse you."
"1346","(1346) Abd ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Sharik, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer; Concerning a man who has yellow saliva coming out, he said: It will not harm him."
"1347","(1347) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I heard Al-Harith Al-Ukli saying: He spits about a man and there is blood in his slugs. He said: If the blood predominates with slugs, then ablution is required."
"1348","(1348) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of his leaders, who said: If blood appears on a slug, perform ablution."
"1349","(1349) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Aisha, on the authority of Omar, who said: He washes Urine twice."
"1350","(1350) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man who urinates and splashes it on his thighs and legs. He said: He sprinkles it with water."
"1351","(1351) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id bin Al-Musayyab, he said: Spraying by spraying, pouring by pouring."
"1352","(1352) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: One or two wipes with urine."
"1353","(1353) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwa, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Aisha, she said: She came to Fatima, his son. Abu Hubaysh went to the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, and she said: O Messenger of God, I am a woman who has had her menstruation, but I will not be clean. Should I stop praying? He said: No, that is a blood clot and not menstruation. When menstruation begins, give up prayer, and when it has finished, wash yourself. Blood and prayers. (Bukhari 228, Abu Dawud 286)"
"1354","(1354) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Habib bin Abi Thabit, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Fatima bin Abi Hubaysh came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: O Messenger of God, I am a woman. I have menstruation but I am not clean, should I stop praying? He said: No, that is a sweat and not menstruation. Avoid prayer during the days of your menstruation, then wash yourself and perform ablution for all Pray, then pray, even if blood drips on the mat. (Abu Dawud 302 and Ibn Majah 624)"
"1355","(1355) Ibn Numayr and Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Sulayman ibn Yasar, on the authority of Umm She greeted him, she said: A woman asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she said: I am menstruating but do not feel clean, should I give up prayer? He said: No, but leave the number of days and nights that you were menstruating and their number, then wash yourself, ask for forgiveness, and pray. However, Ibn Numayr said: Umm Salama consulted the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: A woman who sheds blood? He said: She waits for the number of days and nights during which she was menstruating, or for a number of months, then he mentioned something like the hadith of my father. Osama\n(Abu Dawud 278 and Ibn Majah 623)"
"1356","(1356) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Ikrimah; The mother of your beloved, the son of Jahsh, underwent menstruation, so she asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, or was he asked about her? So he ordered her to look at the days of her days, then wash herself, and if she saw anything after that, she should perform ablution, refresh herself, and pray. (Abu Dawud 309. Al-Bayhaqi 351)"
"1357","(1357) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Suleiman Ibn Yasar; That Fatima bin Abi Hubaysh had her menstruation, so she asked the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, or was he asked about her? So he ordered her to give up prayer on the days of her prayers, then to wash herself during other days, then to remove a garment and pray. (Daraqutni 10)"
"1358","(1358) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abu Ja’far; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, commanded the woman in need, when the days of her reading had passed, to wash and perform ablution for every prayer. And you pray."
"1359","(1359) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; That a stolen woman asked Aisha about the woman who needs menstruation? She said: Perform ablution for every prayer and stand alone and pray."
"1360","(1360) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Al-Mujalid, and Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: You sent your wife to another woman. Stolen. So I asked her about the woman who is in need of menstruation, and she mentioned on the authority of Aisha that she said: She sits for the days of her menstruation, then she takes a bath. And perform ablution for every prayer."
"1361","(1361) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’ bin Hakim, he said: I asked Saeed bin Al-Musayyab About the woman suffering from menstruation? He said: No one is more knowledgeable about this than me. When her menstruation begins, let her give up prayer, and when it ends, let her wash herself, and let her wash off her robes. blood, and perform ablution for every prayer."
"1362","(1362) Hafs and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, who said: The woman who is in need of menstruation should bathe and perform ablution for every... Pray"
"1363","(1363) Hatem told us, on the authority of Abdul Rahman bin Harmala, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; In a woman who is menstruating, and her menstrual cycle overtakes her, she washes and cleanses herself, then she makes a kursuf as a shepherd makes. You cover yourself with a garment, then you pray."
"1364","(1364) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: You delay the noon prayer and hasten it. Asr, and you bathe once, and you delay Maghrib and sooner for Isha, and you bathe once, then you bathe until dawn, Then you compare them."
"1365","(1365) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: She sits during the days of her menstruation, which she used to menstruate. So, when those days have passed, she bathes, then she delays the noon prayer and hastens the afternoon prayer, then she performs them both with one bath. Each one of them at its own time, then to wash for Maghrib and Isha, and to delay Maghrib and sooner than for Isha, then pray Each one of them at a certain time, then she takes a bath at dawn."
"1366","(1366) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: You bathe from the back. To noon."
"1367","(1367) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Sumayyah, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab, the same."
"1368","(1368) Muhammad bin Zayd told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, on the authority of his followers, that Ali and Ibn Abbas said regarding Al-Muḍadhaad: She takes a bath for every prayer."
"1369","(1369) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, who said: You bathe at noon and afternoon. A ritual ablution, and a ritual ablution for Maghrib and Isha, and a ritual ablution for dawn."
"1370","(1370) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, he said: I was with Ibn Abbas. Then a woman came with a letter and she read it, and behold, in it was a woman who was undergoing menstruation, and Ali said: She should bathe for every prayer. Ibn Abbas said: I do not find anything for her except what Ali said."
"1371","(1371) Hafs bin Ghayath narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ali; Concerning the one who is suffering from istihaadah, you delay the noon prayer and hasten the afternoon prayer, and you delay the sunset prayer and hasten the evening prayer. He said: And I think so. He said: And you wash yourself at dawn. He said: So I mentioned that to Ibn al-Zubayr and Ibn Abbas, and they said: We do not find anything about her except what Ali said."
"1372","(1372) Safwan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Othman Al-Makhzoumi, who said: I asked Salim and Al-Qasim about Al-Mustahadha, One of them said: She waits for the days of her prayers, so when the days of her prayers have passed, she washes and prays, and the other said: She takes a bath from Back to back"
"1373","(1373) Zayd bin Harun narrated to us, saying: A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Muhammad bin Aqeel, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhammad bin Talhah, on the authority of his uncle Imran bin Talhah, on the authority of his mother Hamna ibn Jahsh; She underwent menstruation at the time of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and she came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. She said: O Messenger of God, I had a very bad menstruation, so he said to her: Eat a piece of celery. She said: It is More severe than that, I am more bitter than that. He said: Bridle and menstruate in every month, according to the knowledge of God, six days, or seven days. Then take a bath, and pray and fast on the twenty-third or twenty-fourth, and the end of the noon and the beginning of the afternoon, and take a bath. Perform a ritual ablution for them, finish the Maghrib prayer, serve the evening prayer, and perform a ritual ablution for them. This is the most beloved of the two things to me. (Ibn Majah 627 Abu Dawud 291)"
"1374","(1374) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Yaqzan, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of his father, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He said: The woman suffering from menstruation should leave prayer on the days of her recitation, then she should bathe, perform ablution for every prayer, and fast. And you pray.\n(Abu Dawud 301, Tirmidhi 126)"
"1375","(1375) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Yaqzan, on the authority of Adiy ibn Thabit, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ali, the same."
"1376","(1376) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, saying: Ismail narrated to me, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Abd Allah; He heard Abu Ja`far say regarding the woman who is in need of menstruation: It is only an attack from Satan, so if she is overcome by blood, she should cleanse herself and take a bath. After reciting it, he performed ablution, as Aisha said."
"1377","(1377) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Anas Ibn Sirin, who said: A woman from the family of Anas underwent menstruation. So they ordered me to ask Ibn Abbas? He said: If she sees blood in her body, she should not pray, but if she sees pure blood, even if it is for an hour during the day, she should wash and pray."
"1378","(1378) Abdul bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Zainab bint Umm Salama, she said: I saw His son is a colt, and she was undergoing istihaadah. She comes out of the place and the blood is overwhelming, then she prays."
"1379","(1379) Mu’tamir bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: You take a bath from the noon prayer to the same time as before. Tomorrow"
"1380","(1380) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He made this rain, and he knew that he would perform ablution with it using black and white ones. He said: He was pouring from The people's ablution was inside her, so she asked for a gift? He said: There is no harm in it."
"1381","(1381) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Raja’, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Al-Bara’ bin Azib He urinated, then he came to the mosque’s toilet and performed ablution there."
"1382","(1382) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Issa bin Al-Mughirah, who said: I asked Saeed bin Jubayr about the raincoat that Do people put their hands into it? He said: Water does not make anything impure."
"1383","(1383) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Uthman ibn Al-Aswad, who said: Mujahid used to perform ablution from the ablution of the people."
"1384","(1384) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismah bin Zamil, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; He performed ablution from the purifier."
"1385","(1385) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muzahim, who said: I said to al-Sha`bi: I would like to perform ablution with old, fermented cobs. From it, or the basin into which the butcher puts his hand? He said: From the purifier that the butcher puts his hand into."
"1386","(1386) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Salih, on the authority of Sa`id bin Abdullah bin Dirar, on the authority of his father, he said: Do not perform ablution from the toilet bowl that is in the market, when Abdullah came and said: Here, where is your sleep today? He said: I said: In the Levant."
"1387","(1387) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, who said: I said to Ata’: I saw a man performing ablution in that basin. Exposed? He said: There is no problem with it, Ibn Abbas made it, and he knew that one can perform ablution with it, both white and black."
"1388","(1387) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of some Bani Mudlij; He asked the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he said: O Messenger of God, we ride rafts in the sea for fishing. So we carry water with us to heal ourselves, so when the time for prayer comes, if one of us performs ablution with his own water, he will be thirsty, and if he performs ablution with sea water, he will find In himself? He claimed that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The pure is its water, and its dead body is lawful."
"1389","(1389) Abd al-Rahim narrated to us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Amr ibn Dinar, on the authority of Abu al-Tufayl, he said: Abu Bakr Al-Siddiq, should he perform ablution with sea water? He said: The pure is its water, and the lawful is its dead matter."
"1390","(1390) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Yazid al-Madani, he said: One of the fishermen told me, he said: When Omar came to the neighbor Commander of the Faithful, seeking food for sustenance. He said: I said: O Commander of the Faithful; We are riding our rafts, and we carry with us water for healing. Some people claim that sea water does not purify oneself, so he said: What water? Purer than him."
"1391","(1391) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of Ikrimah; That Omar was asked about sea water? He said: What water is purer than this?"
"1392","(1392) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub, on the authority of Qatadī, on the authority of Sinan bin Salamah; Did he ask Ibn Abbas about sea water? He said: With two heats, it will not harm you whichever one you performed ablution with. Sea water and Euphrates water."
"1393","(1393) Abdul Rahim told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Sea game is lawful, and its water is birds."
"1394","(1394) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: There is no harm in performing ablution from sea water."
"1395","(1395) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said: There is no harm in it, it is pure."
"1396","(1396) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Ghayath, on the authority of Ikrimah; He was asked about sea water, should he perform ablution with it? He said: Should we not eat its whales?"
"1397","(1397) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, who said: Sea water removes dirt from He changed it, and he saw it as pure."
"1398","(1398) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Zubayr ibn Adiyy, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Sea water suffices, And sweet is more beloved to me than that."
"1399","(1399) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Sea water is pure."
"1400","(1400) Waki’ told us, on the authority of his people, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa’id ibn al-Musayyab, who said: If you seek refuge in him, there is no problem. With it"
"1401","(1401) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, on the authority of Amr bin Saad al-Jari, who said: Omar came The neighbor called for handkerchiefs and said: Wash yourself in the sea water, for it is blessed."
"1402","(1402) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Safwan bin Sulaym, on the authority of Sa’id bin Salama, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Abi Burda heard Abu Hurairah say: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The pure sea. Its water, lawful is its death. (Abu Dawud 84. Tirmidhi 69)"
"1403",""
"1404","(1404) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr, who said Sea water does not suffice for ablution or ritual ritual impurity. Indeed, under the sea is fire, then water, then fire."
"1405","(1405) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham al-Dastawai, on the authority of Yahya ibn Abi Kathir, on the authority of a man from the Ansar On the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: Two waters are not sufficient for washing the ritual impurity. Sea water and pigeon water."
"1406","(1406) Ishaq bin Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ja`far, on the authority of Al-Rabi’ bin Anas, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah; He sailed into the sea and ran out of water, so he performed ablution with wine, but he did not like to perform ablution with sea water."
"1407","(1407) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Yazid al-Dalani, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu al-Aliya, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Whoever sleeps prostrate is not required to perform ablution until he lies down. When he lies down, the body becomes relaxed. joints (Ahmad 1/256; Abu Ali 2487)"
"1408","(1408) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas, who said: The companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace They bow their heads and wait for dinner, then they get up and pray, but they do not perform ablution. (Abu Dawud 2020 Tirmidhi 78)"
"1409","(1409) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mughirah ibn Ziyad, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Whoever falls asleep while sitting, does not Ablution is performed on him, and if he lies down, then the ablution is required."
"1410","(1410) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to sleep in He bows and prostrates, then prays, but does not perform ablution."
"1411","(1411) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, slept in the mosque. Until he blew, then he stood up and prayed without performing ablution, and he said: The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, his eyes sleep, but he does not sleep. His heart"
"1412","(1412) Hafs told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; He did not consider anyone who slept sitting to perform ablution."
"1413",""
"1414","(1414) Zayd ibn al-Hubab told us, he said: Malik ibn Anas informed me, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, that Omar ibn Al-Khattab said: Whoever lays on his side, let him perform ablution."
"1415","(1415) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun. And Ibn Idris, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, said: I asked Ubaidah about him? He said: He knows best about himself."
"1416","(1416) Hushaym told us, saying: Abdul-Malik told us, on the authority of Ata’, that he said: He who sleeps prostrate, or standing, or If he is sitting, then he does not have to perform ablution, but if he sleeps lying down, then he does not have to perform ablution."
"1417","(1417) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, the same thing."
"1418","(1418) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, on the authority of Ikrimah; He saw no harm in sleeping while sitting, and he hated it while lying down."
"1419","(1419) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, he said: I saw Ibn Sirin shaking his head, then getting up and praying."
"1420","(1420) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was He, peace and blessings be upon him, sleeps until it is blown, then he gets up and prays without performing ablution. (Ibn Majah 474 and Ibn Rahwi 1490)"
"1421","(1421) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: Al-Hikam and Hammad mentioned him, and they said: He is not required to perform ablution until he performs the ritual prayer. beside him"
"1422","(1422) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If a man sleeps standing or sitting, it is not obligatory He has to perform ablution, so if he places it on his side, it is obligatory for him to perform ablution."
"1423","(1423) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Miqsam, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Ablution is obligatory for everyone who is sleeping except Whoever beats his head one or two times."
"1424","(1424) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Yazid, on the authority of Abu Nadhrah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: I visited my maternal aunt. Maimoonah, and the night of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, fell, so he got up during the night to pray, then he fell asleep, and I heard a whistle. He said: Then Bilal came to call him to prayer, so he went out to pray and did not perform ablution, nor did he touch water."
"1425","(1425) Ishaq bin Mansour narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour bin Abi Al-Aswad, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to sleep while prostrating, and his sleep could not be known except by his blowing, then He gets up and continues his prayer. (Ahmad 1/426, Ibn Majah 475)"
"1426","(1426) Yahya bin Saeed narrated to us, on the authority of Tariq Baya’ al-Nawawi, who said: Mana’i’ bin Waqqas narrated to me, on the authority of Abiya; That Abu Musa used to sleep between them until he fell asleep, so we would alert him, and he would say: Did you hear me? Did I narrate? So we say: No, so he gets up and prays."
"1427","(1427) Hushaym and Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Khalid bin Ghulaq Al-Aishi, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, He said: Whoever deserves to sleep, it is obligatory for him to perform ablution. Ibn Aliyah added: Al-Jariri said: So we asked about the entitlement to sleep? They said: When he is placed on his side."
"1428","(1428) Abdullah bin Idris told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawoos; He was asked about a man who falls asleep while sitting? He said: It is a treacherous place, so if you lose it, That is, he says: he performs ablution."
"1429","(1429) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Omar bin Al-Walid Al-Shinni, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: He is only Waki’, so when he sleeps he performs ablution."
"1430","(1430) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He used to perform ablution on someone who slept while sitting."
"1431","(1431) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, and Amr, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: Whoever falls asleep should perform ablution."
"1432","(1432) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab and al-Hasan. They said: When sleep mingles with his heart He performed ablution standing or sitting."
"1433","(1433) Zayd ibn al-Hubab told us, he said: Malik ibn Anas informed me, he said: Zayd ibn Aslam informed me, that Omar ibn Al-Khattab said: Whoever lays on his side, let him perform ablution."
"1434","(1434) Affan narrated to us, he said: Aban Al-Attar narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father, he said: If he fell asleep heavily While he was sitting, he performed ablution."
"1435","(1435) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymimi, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Suwayd, he said: Abdullah said: Because it is more beloved to me to perform ablution from an evil word than to perform ablution from good food."
"1436","(1436) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Asim bin Abi al-Najjoud, on the authority of Dhakwan Abi Salih, on the authority of Aisha, She said: One of you should perform ablution with good food, but not with an evil word, which he says to his brother."
"1437","(1437) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: I was informed that an old man from the Ansar was passing by. As they sit, he says: Repeat your ablution, for some of what you say is worse than the hadith."
"1438","(1438) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, I said to Ubaidah: What is ablution repeated from? He said: From the incident, and harming a Muslim."
"1439","(1439) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ajlan, on the authority of Al-Harith, he said: I was holding Ibrahim’s hand and I mentioned A man and I backbited him. He said: So he said to me: Go back and perform ablution. They used to consider this a form of slander."
"1440","(1440) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Al-Furat, who said: Two men asked Ata’ and he said: A man passed by us. So we said: The effeminate. He said: Did you say to him before you prayed, or after you prayed? They said: Before we pray, and he said: Perform ablution and return to your prayer, for you have not prayed together."
"1441","(1441) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq; That Abu Salih recited a poem containing a satire, so he called for water and rinsed his mouth."
"1442","(1442) Omar bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, who said: I asked Al-Zuhri regarding some matter regarding ablution. Poetry and other things? He said: No."
"1443","(1443) Al-Fadl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, on the authority of Abu Al-Aliyah, who said: It is not in talking, cursing, and making noise. Ablution"
"1444","(1444) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say regarding the kasra when it was forced into a ta’ara: Wipe. After that, upon him."
"1445","(1445) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’, that he used to say regarding a kasra when it was forced: He wipes over it. Splints"
"1446","(1446) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Taymi, who said: I asked a peacock about a wound on a man’s face, or on some part of it. Is his body wearing medicine or a rag? He said: If he is afraid, he can wipe over the rag, and if he is not afraid, he can remove the rag."
"1447","(1447) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim and Daoud, on the authority of Abu Al-Aaliyah; He complained about his foot, so he bandaged it, performed ablution, wiped over it, and said: She is sick."
"1448","(1448) Muadh told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, he said: I had a wound from the plague, so I asked Abu Majliz, and he said: Wipe it. Aliyah"
"1449","(1449) Wakī’ narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bā, on the authority of Amr ibn Murā, on the authority of Yusuf ibn Mahak, on the authority of Ubaid ibn Umair; Concerning a man who has a wound, he said: He should wash himself and wash what is around him."
"1450","(1450) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Abd al-A’la, on the authority of Suwayd ibn Ghafla, who said: He erases what around him"
"1451","(1451) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, and Al-Hasan that they used to say: He wipes over splints."
"1452","(1452) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, who said: A calamity befell me, and he fell ill. The fork of his finger was at the beginning of his eyebrow, so I tied a bandage over him, so I asked Saeed bin Jubair, should I wipe over him? He said: Yes."
"1453","(1453) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Amr bin Murra, on the authority of Yusuf bin Mahak, he said: It was revealed to us A guest had a wet dream and had a wound, so we came to Ubaid bin Umair and mentioned that to him, and he said: He washes what is around him, but he does not Water touches him."
"1454","(1454) Ibn Abi Ghaniyy told us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of the ruling, he said: If it is on the hand or the foot that is wounded. So he feared for his companion if water got on him. He wiped over the rag when he performed ablution."
"1455","(1455) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ash’ath ibn Abi Ash-Sha’tha’i, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: He wipes over it, for God excuses with excuse."
"1456","(1456) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Hassan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: A man wipes if he fears for him. Himself"
"1457","(1457) Mu’tamar bin Imran told us, on the authority of Abu Majliz, that he said: He wipes over it."
"1458","(1458) Shabab narrated to us, he said: Hisham bin Al-Ghaz narrated to us, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Whoever has a bandaged wound So there is fear of curse upon him, so let him wipe what is around him and not wash it."
"1459","(1459) Abdi told us, on the authority of Ibn Abjar, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He wipes over the veins."
"1460","(1460) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Al-Aizar, on the authority of Talq ibn Habib, he said: Omar ibn Al-Khattab saw A man scratched his armpit or touched it, and he said to him: Get up and wash your hand or purify yourself."
"1461","(1461) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, he said: Omar said: Whoever cleans his nose, or touches his armpits He performed ablution."
"1462","(1462) Khalaf bin Khalifa told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: There is no ablution in plucking the armpit."
"1463","(1463) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a man who touched his nose and plucked his armpits? He did not see any harm in it, unless he bloodied it."
"1464","(1464) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: These people say: Whoever touches his armpits repeats the ablution. And I say that, but I do not know what this is."
"1465","(1465) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abdullah bin Amr; He used to take a bath by plucking his armpits."
"1466","(1466) Abu Khalid narrated to us, not by Al-Ahmar, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Awn bin Abdullah bin Utbah and Al-Zuhri said: If a man touches his armpit, he should repeat the ablution."
"1467","(1467) Hushaym narrated to us, Al-Mughirah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: If blood drips, the ablution is invalidated."
"1468","(1468) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He did not use any blood to perform ablution except what was liquid."
"1469","(1469) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid; He was asked about a man who had blood coming out of his hand, but the blood did not go beyond its place? He said: He performs ablution."
"1470","(1470) Yahya bin Ali al-Taymi told us, on the authority of Mansour; Did he ask Abraham about that? He said: He should not perform ablution until he comes out."
"1471","(1471) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If blood emerges from the nose and becomes visible, then ablution is required."
"1472","(1472) Ismail bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I heard Al-Sha’abi say: Ablution It is obligatory for every flowing blood.\n He said: And I heard the ruling saying: From every flowing blood."
"1473","(1473) Abu Bakr said: I heard Ibn Idris saying: I heard Malik bin Anas saying: Ablution is not performed except from the two paths; Feces and urine."
"1474","(1474) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He put his fingers into his nose and blood came out, so he wiped it and prayed, but he did not perform ablution."
"1475","(1475) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, on the authority of Mujahid, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; He did not see any harm in one or two drops of blood during prayer."
"1476","(1476) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of Abu Qalab; He saw no harm in discord and blood coming out of it."
"1477","(1477) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; He saw nothing wrong with blood coming out of a man's nose, if he were able to squirt it with his finger unless it would flow out. Or it drips."
"1478","(1478) Abdul Wahhab told us, on the authority of Al-Taymiy, on the authority of Bakr, he said: I saw Ibn Umar squeeze a pimple on his face and he came out. There was some blood, so he rubbed it between his two fingers, then prayed, but did not perform ablution."
"1479","(1479) Ubayd Allah ibn Musa told us, on the authority of Hanzala, on the authority of Tawus; He did not consider the flowing blood to be an ablution to wash away the blood, then he considered it sufficient for him."
"1480","(1480) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Ala’, he said: I asked Sa’id bin Jubayr, and I said: I perform ablution and take the bucket. So I draw water with it and the rope scratches me, or does I get scratched and blood comes out of it? He said: Wash it and do not perform ablution."
"1481","(1481) Shababi told us, he said: Shu’ba told us, on the authority of Ghaylan bin Jami’, on the authority of Maymun bin Mihran, he said: He told us Whoever sees Abu Hurairah inserting his fingers into his nose, and blood comes out on it, wipes it, then gets up and prays."
"1482","(1482) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Ubaid Allah bin Habib bin Abi Thabit narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; He put his finger into his nose and blood came out on it, so he wiped it with the ground, or with dirt, then prayed."
"1483","(1483) Harami bin Amara narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Khalda, who said: I saw Abu Sawwar al-Adawi squeeze a blood clot, then he prayed. He did not perform ablution."
"1484","(1484) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father; He used to say to his sons: Do not perform ablution with a boil unless it is bitter."
"1485","(1485) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Saif, who said: His mujahid had ulcers that were oozing, and he did not perform ablution. And his clothes are stained and he does not wash them."
"1486","(1486) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Qaqa’, he said: I said to Ibrahim: There is a man with many boils, and they do not stop bleeding? He said: He washes her place, performs ablution, and hastens to pray."
"1487","(1487) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khaled, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi; He was asked about a man with a fistula? He said: He prays even if it drips from his horn to his feet."
"1488","(1488) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; Concerning a man praying with a thick garment on him. He said: He should not wash him until he is healed. If he is healed, he should wash his garment. He said: I saw Ibrahim praying, and there was some pus on his garment from Habon that was on it."
"1489","(1489) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Umayyah, who said: I saw a peacock praying and it was as if his garment was covered with sores. With her legs"
"1490","(1490) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: He performs ablution."
"1491","(1491) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hayyan al-Jawfi, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: He performs ablution."
"1492","(1492) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Abi Nabati, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: He performs ablution."
"1493","(1493) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Concerning a woman and a man, something comes out of them after they have done ablution. He said: They wash their private parts and perform ablution."
"1494","(1494) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Aroub and others, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who takes a bath from ritual impurity, then some semen comes out of his penis. He said: If he urinated before he He takes a bath and does not wash again, but if he did not wet himself, then he should wash again."
"1495","(1495) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked Al-Hakam and Hammad about a man who takes a bath from ritual impurity. So the thing comes out of his remembrance? They said: He should wash his penis."
"1496","(1496) Ibn Al-Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir bin Zayd in the mirror. Some of the man’s semen comes out of her after washing. He said: She has to perform ablution."
"1497","(1497) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Rabi’i bin Harash, who said: Salman said: If one of you tells the story His skin, do not wipe it with a slug, for a slug is not pure."
"1498","(1498) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, he said: It was said to him: Did Abraham hate slugs? He said: He only hated for a man to scratch his skin and then follow his saliva, for that is not a ritual purification."
"1499","(1499) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim; He hates letting slugs get on the sore."
"1500","(1500) Zajir bin Al-Salt narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Harith bin Malik, who said: I went to Al-Hasan’s house and a man came to him and asked him, and he said: O Abu Saeed: A man scratches either his body or his arms, then he applies his saliva on it, so he wipes it over it. Does he perform ablution with it? He said: No."
"1501","(1501) Saeed bin Yahya Al-Himyari narrated to us, saying: Abu Al-Ala narrated to us, saying: We were with his leaders, so they remembered With the words of Ibrahim and the words of the coffin in slugs: to be washed, he said: So his commander scratched his leg, then he took some of his saliva. Something, then He ordered it to show us that it was nothing."
"1502","(1502) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Abu Harun al-Ghanawi, on the authority of Abu Majliz, who said: Ibn Umar said: If If one of you took a bath after ritual impurity and urinated before he finished his bath, he should pour the water over his head."
"1503","(1503) Ibn Mubarak narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Harun, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: He celebrates Eid, meaning: Washing"
"1504","(1504) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Yahya ibn Atiq, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: He does not return to Repeated washing."
"1505","(1505) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith bin Abi Sulaym, on the authority of Ata’; He said: He is in a state of impurity. He goes to the well and does not have a vessel with him. He said: He lets his garment fall into the well, then squeezes it. On his body."
"1506","(1506) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; He was asked about a junub man who went to Al-Ghadir? He said: He takes a bath in one part of it."
"1507","(1507) Ali bin Hashim narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: We used to recommend it. To take some of the stream's water and wash ourselves with it in a nearby area."
"1508","(1508) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God forbade May God bless him and grant him peace, not to urinate in stagnant water. (Muslim 94. An-Nasa’i 35)"
"1509","(1509) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, who said: None of you should urinate in water. The permanent one, then he washes from it."
"1510","(1510) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Salama ibn Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: He does not One of you is in standing water, then purifies himself from it."
"1511","(1511) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Ibn Ajlan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: May God bless him and grant him peace: None of you should urinate in standing water, nor should he bathe in it from his ritual impurity. (Abu Dawud 71. Ahmad 2/433)"
"1512","(1512) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Mu’awiyah ibn Salih informed us, saying: Abu Maryam informed me, on the authority of my father. Huraira, that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: None of you should urinate in stagnant water, then perform ablution. From him (Ahmed 532)"
"1513","(1513) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ka’b, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Abdul Rahman Ibn Rafi’ Ibn Khadij, on the authority of Abu Sa’id Al-Khudri, it was said: O Messenger of God, I will perform ablution from my well. He said: And... A well into which menstruation, dog meat, and rotten things are thrown. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The water is pure, not pure. Something makes him impure. (Abu Dawud 68. Tirmidhi 66)"
"1514","(1514) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Awf Al-Arabi, he said: He narrated to us in the council of sheikhs before Ibn Al-Ash’ath occurred. An old man, who was telling the story to us, said: I was informed that the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, were on a journey. So they came to Ghadir, on the side of which was a cave, and they held off on it until the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came to them. He greeted him, and they said: O Messenger of God, there is a grave near him, and he said: Water and draw water, for water is permissible, but it is not It is forbidden. (Bayhaqi 258)"
"1515","(1515) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, passed by in Ghadir. They said: O Messenger of God, dogs gnaw on it, as do wild lions. So the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The lion has what it takes. His stomach, and the dog has what he took into his stomach, so drink and perform ablution. He said: So they drank and performed ablution. (Bayhaqi 258)"
"1516","(1516) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Maymun ibn Abi Shabib; Omar bin Al-Khattab passed by the basin of Majnah and said: Give me a drink from it. They said: It is attacked by wild beasts, dogs and donkeys. So he said: For them is what they carried in their bellies: and what remains is for us purification and drink."
"1517","(1517) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Ikrimah; Omar bin Al-Khattab came to a menstrual basin and wanted to perform ablution and drink, so the people of the basin said: It is urinating in it. Dogs and wild animals. Omar said: Indeed, they have something that gnaws in their bellies. He said: So he drank and performed ablution."
"1518","(1518) Sufyan Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of an outcast, on the authority of his mother; She was traveling with Maimunah, and she passed by a stream in which there were camels and camels, and he would draw water for her from it, and she would perform ablution. And you drink."
"1519","(1519) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Habib Ibn Shihab, on the authority of his father; He asked Abu Hurairah about the secrets of the basin that wild beasts would throw away and a donkey would drink from it? He said: Nothing is forbidden from water."
"1520","(1520) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan, he said: Ka’b bin Abdullah narrated to us, he said: We were with Hudhayf, so we came to a cave in which there was the dead, and the menstruating woman took a bath in it, and he said: Water does not prevent one from avoiding ritual impurity."
"1521","(1521) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: Water is pure and no one can make it impure except the impure one, meaning: The polytheist"
"1522","(1522) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Water does not avoid water."
"1523","(1523) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Abu Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, who said: The water does not Something makes him impure."
"1524","(1524) Waki` told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of al-Jariri, on the authority of someone who heard Sa`id ibn al-Musayyab say: Water does not make one impure. Something"
"1525","(1525) Zaid bin Al-Miqdam told us, on the authority of his father, Al-Miqdam, on the authority of his grandfather, on the authority of Aisha, she said: It is not He will be surrounded by water."
"1526","(1526) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: God sent down the water to be pure, so nothing would defile it. And perhaps he said: Nothing will make him impure. Dawud said: That is because We asked him about treachery and menstruation in which dogs urinate."
"1527","(1527) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I said to Al-Qasim bin Muhammad: We will go to Al-Ghadir, but he raged about it. The dogs and the donkey drank from it. Shall we drink from it? Ibn Aoun said: Or did I say: Should we perform ablution with it? Then he looked at me and said: When one of you comes to a stream, he waits until he is asked: What kind of dog urinated in it, or what kind of donkey drank from it? This?"
"1528","(1528) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Ibrahim, who said: Al-Hasan was asked about the hidayas that are located on the road to Mecca. What donkeys and wildebeest want? He said: There is no harm in it."
"1529","(1529) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ikrimah, who said: Water is pure and nothing can make it impure."
"1530","(1530) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Amr Al-Bahrani, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: Water is a bird that does not defile it. Something"
"1531","(1531) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Issa bin Al-Mughiryah, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: Water does not make one impure."
"1532","(1532) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Abd Rabbuh, on the authority of Salih; Jabir bin Zayd said to a man: Pour water on me while he was in the bathroom. He said: I am junub, so he said: Get up and wash, for the water does not Something makes him impure."
"1533","(1533) Abd al-Rahim and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ja`far bin al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abd Allah bin Abdullah bin Omar, on the authority of Ibn Omar, said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about water on land. The falcon, and what kind of wild animals and animals are he like? He said: If the water is two drops, it does not carry impurity.\n(Abu Dawud 65. Tirmidhi 67)"
"1534","(1534) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Walid ibn Kathir, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ja’far ibn Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Abdullah, on the authority of Ibn Umar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, like him, or something similar. (Ibn Hibban 1249)"
"1535","(1535) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Amr, who said: If the water Forty few, nothing made him impure."
"1536","(1536) Ishaq Al-Azraq narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna, on the authority of Salama bin Wharam, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: So The water was two sins and nothing made it impure."
"1537","(1537) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Asim ibn al-Mundhir, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: When the water reaches two hundred, you should not Carrying an unclean thing. Or a word similar to it."
"1538","(1538) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad, who said: If the water reaches the point of forming a pool, it will not be carried. unclean"
"1539","(1539) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Yazid, on the authority of Masruq, who said: If the water is hard, then do not Something defiles him."
"1540","(1540) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi al-Furat, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Sa`id ibn Jubayr, who said: Water A person who is stagnant is not made impure by anything as long as it is three small amounts."
"1541","(1541) Yazeed told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: If the water is two quarts, nothing will defile it. A partner said: I said to Abu Ishaq: What is meant by the two qalatayn? He said: The two jars."
"1542","(1542) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: If the water is crystalline, nothing will make it impure."
"1543","(1543) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad ibn al-Munkadir, who said: When the water reaches forty, a little does not Something makes him impure. Or a word similar to it."
"1544","(1544) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They used to touch henna after the light, and they They hate that he affects the nails."
"1545","(1545) Abd ibn Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; Concerning henna and good manners for a man after the light, he said: As for henna, there is no problem, but as for good manners, I hate it."
"1546","(1546) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of his father, who said: I had a debt on Al-Hasan bin Ali. So I went to him to pay my debts and found him coming out of the bathroom, his nails stained with henna, and his female servant talking about him. Henna in a bottle."
"1547","(1547) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: They hated to be daubed with wine after the light."
"1548","(1548) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Harim, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked, on the authority of Dardiyy. Is it appropriate to rub alcohol with it in the bathroom, or to treat wounds with some of it, or something else? He said: It is an abomination, and God Almighty has commanded one to avoid it."
"1549","(1549) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Yahya bin Abbad, he said: Abu Darda’ came out of He urinated in the mosque, then entered and spoke with its companions, but did not touch water."
"1550","(1550) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yahya Ibn Abi Ishaq, he said: I heard this, I think it happened before Ibn Al-Ash'ath, that Ali urinated, then passed through the mosque before performing ablution."
"1551","(1551) Ali bin Musir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: There is no harm in entering the mosque on Other than ablution."
"1552","(1552) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: Abu Al-Sawwar hated that a man deliberately He sits in the mosque without performing ablution."
"1553","(1553) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Khaled; He said: Abu Ad-Duha used to urinate, then he would enter the Grand Mosque and speak to us."
"1554","(1554) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Jabir ibn Zaid; He used to come from the funeral, then sit in the mosque before performing ablution."
"1555","(1555) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Saeed, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, and Al-Hasan; Concerning a man who said: He passes through the mosque, but does not sit in it."
"1556","(1556) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: There is no harm in him sitting in it in a different way. Ablution"
"1557","(1557) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, he said: I asked the ruling about a man who sits in the mosque without performing ablution? He said: I am the Hour."
"1558","(1558) Ibn Numayr narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, who said: I saw Ibn Sirin coming from the event, so he sat down and took his feet out of the room. The mosque"
"1559","(1559) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Al-Nazzal Al-Asri told us, he said: I saw Khalid Abu Sulaiman. He urinated, then he entered the Bani Asr Mosque and sat down."
"1560","(1560) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir, who said: A person who is in a state of ritual impurity was passing by in the mosque."
"1561","(1561) Hushaym told us, on the authority of the common people; That Ali was passing by the mosque while he was standing next to him, and some of our companions said to him: Did you hear this? He said: I heard it close to fifty years ago."
"1562","(1562) Sharik bin Abdullah narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Karim, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: Junubah passes through The mosque, and he should not sit in it. Then he recited: “And not in a state of ritual impurity, except those passing by.”"
"1563","(1563) A partner told us, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Saeed. And on the authority of Simak, on the authority of Ikrimah, the same."
"1564","(1564) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; {And no one who is in a state of ritual impurity, except those passing through the path} He said: A person who is in a state of ritual impurity does not pass through the mosque unless he finds no other way."
"1565","(1565) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He said: A woman in a state of sexual impurity and a menstruating woman may pass through the mosque, but should not stay there."
"1566","(1566) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, the author of Ad-Distawai, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: The one who is in a state of impurity passes In the mosque, and do not sit in it."
"1567","(1567) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Zayd bin Aslam, who said: A man among them used to become junub, then He performs ablution, then enters the mosque and sits there."
"1568","(1568) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’; In the words of God Almighty: {And no one who is in a state of ritual impurity except those crossing the path} He said: The one who is in a state of ritual impurity passes through the mosque."
"1569","(1569) Humaid bin Abdul Rahman told us, on the authority of Zuhair, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Abu Ad-Duha, on the authority of Masruq; He said: A person in a state of ritual impurity should not pass through the mosque unless he seeks refuge in it."
"1570","(1570) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Bakr bin Abdullah, who said: I said to Al-Hasan: The impurity will befall me, so I will continue. The mosque, and it was taken from the house of Abdullah bin Umair? He said: Rather, go closer if it is closer."
"1571","(1571) Hushaym and Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Anas; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went around his wives one night with one ablution. (Abu Dawud 220; Ibn Hibban 1206)"
"1572","(1572) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salamah, on the authority of Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his paternal aunt, on the authority of Abu Rafi’; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went around to his wives during the night, and he washed himself in the presence of each of their women. So I said: O Messenger of God, if you took one bath? He said: This is purer and more delicious, or purer and cleaner.\n(Abu Dawud 221. Ahmad 6/10)"
"1573","(1573) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Muhammad, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said May God bless him and grant him peace: Suleiman bin Dawud said: I will encircle the night around a hundred women, and each of them will give birth to a boy. He strikes with the sword in the way of God. (Ahmad 2/506)"
"1574","(1574) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Saad bin Malik went around nine of his neighbors in one night, then he stayed for the tenth, and she stayed up and slept, so she was ashamed to wake him up."
"1575","(1575) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; He did not think there was anything wrong with a man washing his hands with some flour or wheat flour."
"1576","(1576) Abu Asama narrated to us, on the authority of Zaida, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, who said: I ate fish with Abraham, so he called I had a stalk, so I washed my hands."
"1577","(1577) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Hammad; He did not see any harm in it, and he said: He hated his corruption."
"1578","(1578) Zayd ibn Harun told us, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Amr ibn Harim, who said: Jabir ibn Zayd was asked about the man. Does he wash his hands with flour and bread from being soaked? He said: There is no problem with that."
"1579","(1579) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Mubarak, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He hated to wash his hands with flour or flour."
"1580","(1580) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Imran bin Hudayr, on the authority of Abu Majliz; He hated it"
"1581","(1581) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Alqamiya; He had a rag with which he used to wipe himself."
"1582","(1582) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Zayd bin Abdullah, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Harith, he said: He had a handkerchief. Wiping with it after ablution."
"1583","(1583) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Khalid, on the authority of Omar bin Ya’li, on the authority of his father, Ali; He did not see anything wrong with wiping the face with a handkerchief after ablution."
"1584","(1584) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail ibn Abi Khaled, on the authority of Hakim ibn Jabir, who said: My father sent a servant of ours to Al-Hasan bin Ali. She saw him performing ablution, so he took a rag after performing ablution and wiped with it. It was as if she hated him. She saw him at night. As if she vomited her liver."
"1585","(1585) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Umm Ghurab, who said: My daughter, a servant of the mother of the sons, the wife of Uthman, narrated to me; Othman performed ablution and wiped his face with a handkerchief."
"1586","(1586) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Suwayd, the client of Amr bin Harith; That Ali took a bath, then took a garment and entered it, meaning: he dried himself with it."
"1587","(1587) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Thabit ibn Ubaid, who said: I saw Bishr ibn Abi Sa’id wiping himself. With a handkerchief."
"1588","(1588) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Ibrahim ibn Muhammad ibn al-Muntashir, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Masruq, that She had a rag to dry herself with."
"1589","(1589) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Muhammad; They did not see any harm in wiping the face with a handkerchief after ablution."
"1590","(1590) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of his father; Al-Hasan and Ibn Sirin did not see any harm in him."
"1591","(1591) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shuabi, on the authority of Asir bin Al-Rabi’ bin Umayla, who said: I saw my father and Abu Al-Ahwas. They wipe with a handkerchief after performing ablution."
"1592","(1592) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ruzaiq, on the authority of Anas; He used to perform ablution and wipe his face and hands."
"1593","(1593) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salim, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, who said: There is no harm in him."
"1594","(1594) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, who said: I asked Al-Hasan about a man who wiped his face with a rag after Does he perform ablution? He said: Yes, as long as the rag is clean."
"1595","(1595) Abdullah bin Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Ajlah, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, that he was asked about the handkerchief after performing ablution; He said: He is a purer face."
"1596","(1596) Ibn Numayr and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, who said: There is no harm in him."
"1597","(1597) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Umar; He wiped his face with his garment."
"1598","(1598) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl, who said: The lions used to wipe themselves. With a handkerchief."
"1599","(1599) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan and Muhammad that they did not see any harm in him, and he was Ibn Sirin says: Leaving him is more beloved to me than him."
"1600","(1600) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; He saw nothing wrong with a man wiping his face with a handkerchief."
"1601","(1601) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Bakr, who said: The most useful thing is a handkerchief in the winter."
"1602","(1602) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Kurayb, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, on the authority of Maymunah; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was brought with a handkerchief, but he did not touch it and started saying: With water like this, meaning: He shakes it off.\n(Muslim 254, An-Nasa’i 250)"
"1603","(1603) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal, on the authority of Ata, on the authority of Jabir; He said: Do not fold your hands when you perform ablution."
"1604","(1604) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: He wipes off the ritual impurity, but does not wipe. From the purification of prayer."
"1605",""
"1606","(1606) Abbad told us, on the authority of Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; He used to hate it and say: You destroyed the handkerchiefs."
"1607","(1607) Mu`tamar narrated to us, on the authority of his father; Abu Al-Aaliyah and Saeed bin Al-Musayyab disliked him wiping his face with a handkerchief after performing ablution."
"1608","(1608) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: They only disliked wearing the handkerchief after ablution. Fear of habit"
"1609","(1609) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Al-Salt bin Bahram, on the authority of Abdul Karim, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; He hated it and said: It will be weighed."
"1610","(1610) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, he said: They said to Salman: Has your Prophet taught you everything, even the nonsense? He said: Yes, he forbade us from facing the Qiblah while defecating or urinating.\n(Abu Dawud 7. Tirmidhi 16)"
"1611","(1611) Shababā told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, on the authority of Ata’ ibn Yazid, on the authority of Abu Ayyub, he said : The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you goes to defecate, he should not face the qiblah, nor should he turn to it. At noon, east, or west. (Bukhari 144. Abu Dawud 9)"
"1612","(1612) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Malik bin Anas, on the authority of Ishaq bin Abdullah bin Abi Talha, on the authority of Rafi’ bin"
"1613","(1613) Khalid bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Suleiman bin Bilal, he said: Amr bin Yahya Al-Mazini narrated to me, on the authority of my father Zaid, on the authority of Maqil al-Asadi, accompanied the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, forbade And he blessed us to face the two qiblahs while defecating or urinating. (Bukhari 1706. Ibn Majah 319)"
"1614","(1614) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Mujahid, who said: It was disliked for the two qiblahs to be faced with urine."
"1615","(1615) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: They hated to face the tribe in a state of excrement. , or urine, or they turn away from it, but from its right, or from its left."
"1616","(1616) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: They hated to receive One of the two qiblahs, while defecating or urinating."
"1617","(1617) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Salamah ibn Wharam, on the authority of Tawus, who said: It is God’s right to honor every Muslim. God accepted it, but He will not receive anything from it. He says: in stool or urine."
"1618","(1618) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Khaled, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Omar bin Abdul-Aziz, who said: I did not receive I have been alone since such-and-such a time."
"1619","(1619) Shababi told us, he said: Laith bin Saad told us, on the authority of Yazid bin Abi Habib; He heard Abdullah bin Al-Harith Al-Zubaidi say: I was the first to hear the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he He says: None of you should urinate in the future, and I will be the first to tell people about it. (Ibn Hibban 14194/Ahmad 191)"
"1620","(1620) Affan told us, he said: Wahib told us, he said: Amr bin Yahya told us, on the authority of Abu Zayd, on the authority of Maqil bin Abi Maqil, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; He forbade us to face the two qiblahs while defecating or urinating."
"1621","(1621) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yahya bin Hibban, on the authority of his uncle Wasi’ Ibn Hibban, on the authority of Ibn Umar, said: I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, sitting and relieving himself, heading towards The kiss\n(Bukhari 1491 Muslim 224)"
"1622","(1622) Al-Thaqafi narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid, on the authority of a man, on the authority of Irrak ibn Malik, on the authority of Aisha; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered that he be alone, so he turned around before the qibla, when he heard that the people disliked that. (Ahmad 6/183; Daraqutni 1/60)"
"1623","(1623) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin Salma, on the authority of Khalid al-Hadha, on the authority of Khalid bin Abi al-Salt, on the authority of Aarak bin Malik, On the authority of Aisha, she said: It was mentioned in the presence of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, that some people hated to receive With their private parts towards the Qiblah, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Face your seat towards the Qiblah (Ahmad 1361). Darqutni 7)"
"1624","(1624) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, he said: They said to Salman: Your Prophet has taught you everything, even the heretics. He said: Yes, he has forbidden us from cleansing ourselves with the right hand."
"1625","(1625) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of some of his companions, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Aisha, she said: He was right-handed. The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for his food and prayer, and his left was for anything else. (Ahmed 165)"
"1626","(1626) Hussein bin Ali narrated to us, on the authority of Zayedah, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Musayyab (h) and other than Hussein said: On the authority of Zayedah, on the authority of Al-Musayyab, on the authority of Sawa'i, on the authority of Hafsa, who said: The right hand of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was for his food and drink. And his ritual, his clothing, and his prayer, and it was his left side for everything else. \n(Nasa’i 10599. Tabarani 353)"
"1627","(1627) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his father, he said: Omar said: I only eat with my right hand, and I feel good. In the north"
"1628","(1628) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was said: A man’s right hand is for his food. And his drink, and his mouth is for his mucus, and for cleansing himself."
"1629","(1629) Abdul Rahim bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Mu’adh, on the authority of Aisha, she said: They passed. Your wives are to wash the traces of excrement and urine, for the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to do that. And I feel ashamed of them.\n(Tirmidhi 19. Ahmad 6/236)"
"1630","(1630) Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin; Aisha used to say to the women: Instruct your husbands to clean themselves with water when they exit the defecation."
"1631","(1631) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Dhar, on the authority of Muslim bin Sabra bin Al-Musayyab bin Najabah, on the authority of his paternal aunt. And she was under his shoe. She said: His shoe was cleansing himself with water."
"1632","(1632) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Gandar and Waki`, on the authority of Shu`ba, on the authority of Ata ibn Abi Maimunah; He heard Anas say: The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to enter the toilet, and I and a young boy would carry a container. And a goat, which cleanses itself with water.\n(Bukhari 1520, Muslim 70)"
"1633","(1633) Al-Dahhak ibn Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, he said: Abu Al-Najashi narrated to us, he said: I accompanied Rafi’ ibn Khadij on a journey. So he was cleansing himself with water."
"1634","(1634) Azhar told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Anas bin Sirin; Anas bin Malik entered the open area and called for Tawar and Ashnan."
"1635","(1635) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: It has reached me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not He enters the bathroom unless he performs ablution or touches water."
"1636","(1636) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Abu Salamah; He heard Abu Nadhrah narrating, on the authority of Abu Sa`id, the client of Abu Asid, and he was a Bedouin. He said: He was Abu Asid. When he came to privacy, I brought him water and he cleaned himself of it. Shuabi said: It means: he cleanses himself."
"1637","(1637) Ibn Dukayn told us, on the authority of Qurayh, on the authority of Badil al-Uqaili, on the authority of Mutarrif ibn Abdullah ibn al-Shakhir, who said: A Bedouin told me, he said: I accompanied Abu Dharr, and all of his morals impressed me except one. I said: What is he? He said: Whenever he came out of the toilet, he would clean himself with water."
"1638","(1638) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Ibn Mubarak, on the authority of Muammar, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; Omar ibn al-Khattab was drinking water between two mounts. He said: It made the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, laugh. And they say: He performs ablution like a woman."
"1639","(1639) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir; Anas used to cleanse himself in the basin."
"1640","(1640) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abd al-Hamid bin Jaafar, on the authority of Mujma’ bin Yaqoub bin Mujma’; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said to Awaim bin Sa`id: What is this bird that God praised you? They said: We wash the backs.\n(Ahmad 3/422, Ibn Khuzaymah 83)"
"1641","(1641) Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, saying: Malik bin Mughul narrated to us, saying: I heard Sayyar Abul-Hakam, more than once, He narrated on the authority of Shahr bin Hawshab, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Salam, who said: When the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came On us, meaning: Qabaa. He said: Indeed, God has praised you with goodness regarding birds, so will you not inform me? He said: This means the Almighty’s saying: {In it are men who love to purify themselves, and God loves those who purify themselves} He said: So they said: O Messenger of God Indeed, we find it written for us in the Torah: cleansing ourselves with water."
"1642","(1642) Hafs told us, on the authority of Dawud bin Abi Hind, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, he said: When these verses were revealed, the Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: O people of Quba, what is this pair that God praised you? They said: There is not one of us who does not clean himself with water from the toilets. {Therein are men who love to purify themselves, and God loves those who purify themselves}"
"1643","(1643) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Jafar, on the authority of his father; Verily, these verses were revealed about the people of Quba’: “Among them are men who love to purify themselves, and God loves those who purify themselves.”"
"1644","(1644) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Zaid al-Rashk, on the authority of Muadh, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Be flexible with your husbands. Did she say: Your men, to wash off the traces of the moth, for we are ashamed to order them to do that."
"1645","(1645) Yahya bin Ali told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik bin Umair, who said: Ali said: Indeed, those who were before you They were making full of hay, but you were making a third of it, so fill the stones with water."
"1646","(1646) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Hudhafi, he said: He was asked about istinja’. With water? He said: Then my hands are still stinking."
"1647","(1647) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Al-Aswad and Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd were entering Being alone, they clean themselves with stones, but do not add anything to them, and do not touch water."
"1648","(1648) Hushaym told us, he said: Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Saeed bin Al-Musayyab, he said: It was mentioned to him. Cleansing yourself with water, and he said: This is the purification of women."
"1649","(1649) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham; It was mentioned to him about cleansing himself with water, so he said: You will do better for that, for they used to throw stones at them."
"1650","(1650) Abdī narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Amr ibn Khuzaymah, on the authority of Ammar ibn Khuzaymah, on the authority of Khuzaymah bin Thabit said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said about seeking cleansing with three stones in which there is no Return\n(Abu Dawud 42. Ibn Majah 315)"
"1651","(1651) Hushaym told us, he said: Abu Bishr told us, on the authority of Tawoos, he said: Cleaning oneself with three stones, he said: I said: What if I do not find three stones? He said: Three sticks. I said: What if I do not find three sticks? He said: Three handfuls of dirt."
"1652","(1652) Hushaym narrated to us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, he said: Al-Hikam narrated to us, he said: Cleaning oneself with three stones. That was not sufficient, so five stones were enough."
"1653","(1653) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Ubayd Allah ibn al-Qubtiyya, on the authority of Ibn al-Zubayr; He saw a man washing off a trace of excrement, so he said: What were we doing to him?"
"1654","(1654) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Yazid, on the authority of Salman, some people said to him: The polytheists and they mock: I see your friend and he is even teaching you nonsense? Salman said: Yes, he ordered us not to face the qiblah, nor to clean ourselves without three stones."
"1655","(1655) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: The Messenger of God came out May God’s prayers and peace be upon him for a pilgrim, and he said: Seek for me three stones, so I brought him two stones and dung. So he took the two stones, threw out the dung, and said: It is rubbish. (Tirmidhi 17 Ahmad 1/388)"
"1656","(1656) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Sufyan, on the authority of Jabir, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: He said: If one of you performs the ritual cleansing, let him perform the ritual cleansing three times, meaning: clean himself with cleanliness. (Muslim 213. Ahmad 3/294)"
"1657","(1657) Hammad bin Masadi told us, on the authority of Yazid, the client of Salamah; Salama did not clean himself with water."
"1658","(1658) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: It was Alqamiya and Al-Aswad, or Abdul-Rahman. Ibn Yazid, no more than three stones."
"1659","(1659) Abu Bakr told us, on the authority of Hatim bin Ismail, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of Nafi’, who said: Ibn Umar did not clean himself with water. With water, I used to bring stones of hot water to him, and when they were full, I would go out with them and throw them out, then I would enter their place."
"1660","(1660) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; Al-Aswad and Al-Alqama used to clean themselves with three stones."
"1661","(1661) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Ghayath, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, on the authority of Alqamah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Do not cleanse yourself with bones or dung, for they only increase the number of jinn for your brothers. (Muslim 1500, Tirmidhi 18)"
"1662","(1662) Abd al-Rahim ibn Sulaiman narrated to us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abdullah He said: I went out with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, for a pilgrim, and he said: Bring me something that I can cleanse myself with, and do not bring me near. No way, no return. (Ahmad 1/426)"
"1663","(1663) Waki’ and Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Zayd, on the authority of Salman, he said: He commanded us to clean ourselves, meaning: the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, with three stones that do not contain Awesome, no bone."
"1664","(1664) Ibn Numayr and Abdou told us, on the authority of Hisham ibn Urwah, on the authority of Amr ibn Khuzaymah, on the authority of Amara ibn Khuzaymah, on the authority of Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The search is made with three stones. There is nothing wrong with it."
"1665","(1665) Abd al-Wahhab al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of al-Hasan; He hated it for a man to clean himself with dung, animal dung, or a bone."
"1666","(1666) Hafs told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Mujahid; He hated to clean himself with the stone with which he had cleaned himself."
"1667","(1667) Hafs told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, meaning Ibn Misra, who said: There is no harm if you turn it over, or It's a joke"
"1668","(1668) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sinan al-Barjami, on the authority of a man, on the authority of al-Hasan, who said: There is no harm if the stone is large for him. Letters that you twist and turn and use to cleanse yourself with them."
"1669","(1669) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Malik bin Mughal, on the authority of Talha, on the authority of Mujahid; He hated to be cleaned with what he had been cleaned with."
"1670","(1670) Abd al-A’la told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of al-Shu’bi, he said: It was forbidden for a man to clean himself with a camel or a bone."
"1671","(1671) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Najiyah Abu Khuffaf, on the authority of Ammar, who said: I committed sexual intercourse while I was in camels, and I could not find water, so I wandered with the beast, so I came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and informed him, and he said: Tayammum was sufficient for you from that. (Nasa’i 309. Ahmad 4/263)"
"1672","(1672) Marwan bin Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Aoun, on the authority of Abu Raja’, who said: Imran bin Husayn narrated to us; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey and led the people in prayer, when a man was secluding himself from the people and said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace: What is the matter with you, why do you pray with the people? He said: My body has befallen me, O Messenger of God, and there is no water. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: You must go to the Upper Egypt. It is sufficient for you. (Bukhari 3571, Muslim 312)"
"1673","(1673) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Abu Qalab, on the authority of a man from Banu Aam[corrupt], on the authority of Abu Dhar, on the authority of The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: The good earth is pure as long as there is no water, even if for ten Hajj, then if you find water So he touched your skin. (Abu Dawud 3361, Ahmad 5/180)"
"1674","(1674) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Ruba’i, on the authority of Hudhayfy, who said: The Messenger of God said: May God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Its soil has been made pure for us if we do not find water, meaning: the earth. (Muslim 371. Ahmad 5/383)"
"1675","(1675) Ali bin Hashim told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Al-Manhal, on the authority of Abbad bin Abdullah Wazir, on the authority of Ali; {Nor those in a state of desert, except those crossing a path.} He said: The passer-by who does not find water performs tayammum and prays."
"1676","(1676) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Bukair ibn al-Akhnas, on the authority of al-Hasan ibn Muslim; {Not even a stranger, except those passing through the path}; Unless you are travelers and perform tayammum."
"1677","(1677) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Abu Majliz, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; {And not a person in a state of ritual impurity, except those passing by.} He said: This is the traveler."
"1678","(1678) Ghandar narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Suleiman bin Musa, who said: They are travelers who do not find water."
"1679","(1679) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Al-Aswad, on the authority of Omar, who said: A person in a state of ritual impurity should not perform tayammum unless he He finds the water well."
"1680","(1680) Muhammad bin Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Abdullah said: If you are on a journey and you become junub. Do not pray until you find water, but if you do, then perform tayammum, then pray."
"1681","(1681) Sufyan bin Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Al-Dahhak, who said: Abdullah retracted his statement about Tayammum."
"1682","(1682) Yahya bin Sa’id narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Zubaid, who said: I was in a state of impurity and could not find water, so I asked Abu Atiyya? He said: Do not pray, and I asked Saeed bin Jubayr? He said: Tayammum and pray."
"1683","(1683) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: I was sitting with Abdullah, and Abu Musa, so Abu Musa: O Abu Abd al-Rahman, have you seen that if a man went into a state of impurity and did not find water for a month, what would he do with prayer? Abdullah said: He should not perform tayammum if he does not find water for a month. Abu Musa said: So he is judged by these verses in Surah Tables: {And if you do not find water, then perform tayammum on clean clay.} Then Abdullah said: If this had been permitted for them, they would have doubted it when it got cold. They are required to perform tayammum in the desert. (Muslim 110. Bukhari 347)"
"1684","(1684) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’; He said: Abu Dharr became in a state of impurity, and he was one of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on his three journeys. He came to him after he had finished praying. In the morning, he defecated due to his need, so he turned to him, put his hand in the dirt, and wiped his face and palms."
"1685","(1685) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’; That Ibn Umar performed tayammum in a place of camels, and said: With his hand on the ground, he wiped his face with it, then struck it with what was on the ground. He struck him again, then wiped his hands up to the elbows with them."
"1686","(1686) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayoub, he said: I asked Salim about tayammum? He said: He struck his hand on the ground and wiped his face with it, then he struck his hand on the ground again and wiped it with it. His hands are up to the elbows."
"1687","(1687) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Habib bin Al-Shahid; Did he hear Al-Hasan being asked about tayammum? So he struck the ground with his hand and wiped his face with it, then he struck the ground with his hand again and wiped it. With what His hand extends to the elbows."
"1688","(1688) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Tayammum is a stroke of the face and hands until The elbows. David described to us: He struck his hands on the ground, then shook them out, then wiped his palms with them, then wiped them with them. His face and arms up to the elbows."
"1689","(1689) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, who said: Abu Musa said to Abdullah: Did you not hear Ammar say: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, sent me on a mission, but I was ungrateful and could not find water, so I wallowed in the plain as he had wallowed. The mount, then I came to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and I mentioned that to him, and he said: It was enough for you to say With your hand like this, then he struck the ground once with his hand, then he wiped the left hand over the right, with the appearance of his palm. His face? Abdullah said: Did you not see Omar who was not satisfied with what Ammar said?"
"1690","(1690) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Ibn Abza, on the authority of his father, he said: Ammar said To Omar: Do you not remember a day when we were in such-and-such and such-and-such, and we went into a state of ritual impurity, but we did not find water, so we remained in the dirt, so when we came to The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, we mentioned that to him, and he said: This is enough for you. Then he struck Al-Amash with his hand. He struck you, then blew them, then wiped his face with them and shrouded them."
"1691","(1691) Mu’tamar told us, on the authority of cold, on the authority of alcohol; In tayammum: he strikes the ground with his hands and wipes his face and palms with them."
"1692","(1692) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim; He said: He loved to reach the elbows with tayammum."
"1693","(1693) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He said: Tayammum involves two strokes: a stroke for the face, and a stroke for the arms up to the elbows."
"1694","(1694) Abu Dawud al-Talisi narrated to us, on the authority of Hammad bin al-Ja’d, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Sirin and Salih Abi Al-Khalil, they said: Tayammum on the face and the two hands. Saeed bin Al-Musayyab and Ibn Omar said: The face and the two arms."
"1695","(1695) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi, he said: He was commanded to perform tayammum for that in which he was commanded to perform ghusl, meaning: it is only It is the face and the arms."
"1696","(1696) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of Al-Zuhri, who said: Tayammum is two blows: one blow to the face. And a blow to the hands."
"1697","(1697) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Malik, on the authority of Ammar; He performed tayammum and wiped the dirt with his hands, then shook them off, then wiped his face and hands with them, but did not wipe them. His arms"
"1698","(1698) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ezra, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abd al-Rahman bin Abza, On the authority of his father, on the authority of Ammar, on the authority of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, that he said regarding tayammum: striking the face. And the two palms.\n(Ibn Hibban 1308 and Abu Dawud 331)"
"1699","(1699) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: I saw him hitting the ground with his hands, then He shook them off, then wiped his face with them."
"1700","(1700) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ezra bin Thabit, on the authority of Abu Al-Zubayr, on the authority of Jabir; He struck the ground with his hand once and wiped his face with it, then he struck the ground with them another stroke and wiped his face with them. His arms up to the elbows."
"1701","(1701) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Musa, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: When the verse was revealed Tayammum: I did not know how to do it, so I went to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, but I did not find him, so I went looking for him. So I met him, and when he saw me, he recognized the one I had come to, so he urinated, then he struck the ground with his hand and wiped his face with it. And that is enough for him."
"1702","(1702) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Zam’i, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father; He said that there are two strokes regarding tayammum: a stroke for the face, and a stroke for the arms up to the elbows."
"1703","(1703) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: Perform tayammum for every prayer."
"1704","(1704) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Aamir, who said: No one can pray with tayammum except one prayer."
"1705","(1705) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Nothing invalidates tayammum except an accident."
"1706","(1706) Al-Dahhak bin Mukhlid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Muthanna bin Al-Sabbah, on the authority of Ata’, who said: All prayers are performed by tayammum. It did not happen."
"1707","(1707) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Hammam, on the authority of Aamir al-Ahwal, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Aas, who said: He performs tayammum for every prayer. His leaders used to issue fatwas about that."
"1708","(1708) Umar ibn Harun narrated to us, on the authority of Thawr, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: He should not perform a voluntary prayer by performing tayammum, nor should he perform two prayers. With one tayammum."
"1709","(1709) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Sa`id, on the authority of his followers, who said: It was astonishing for him to perform tayammum for every prayer."
"1710","(1710) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Abu Hanifa, on the authority of Hammad, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The one who is performing tayammum must perform tayammum unless It happens."
"1711","(1711) A partner narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Harith, on the authority of Ali, who said: A person in a state of impurity blames what is between him and another. Time"
"1712","(1712) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, and Ibn Sirin that they said: He should not perform tayammum as long as he wishes. To have access to water at the right time."
"1713","(1713) Omar told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If you are in the city and attending prayer and you do not have water So wait for water, and if you are afraid you will miss the prayer, then perform tayammum and pray."
"1714","(1714) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: The best level: the tillage or: the land of tillage."
"1715","(1715) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: If a man begins to pray, and he does not find water, When he did not reach the ground, he struck his saddle and his cloak with his hand, then performed tayammum with it."
"1716","(1716) Rawad bin Jarrah, Abu Issam, narrated to us, on the authority of Sadiqa bin Yazeed, on the authority of Hammad, who said: He performs tayammum in Upper Egypt. And the plaster, and the mountain, and the sand."
"1717","(1717) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Hammad, who said: Everything that you strike with your hands is on a level ground until Dust for your home."
"1718","(1718) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Israel, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amir, who said: He should perform tayammum using pastures and mountains."
"1719","(1719) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Awf, on the authority of Abu Uthman al-Nahdi, who said: I have been informed that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him And he said: Wipe yourself with it, for it is righteousness for you, meaning: the earth. (Tabarani 416)"
"1720","(1720) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Zam’i bin Salih, on the authority of Issa bin Azdad, on the authority of his father, he said: The Messenger said: God, may God bless him and grant him peace: If any of you urinates, let him sprinkle his penis with three nitrates. (Ahmad 4/347, Ibn Majah 326)"
"1721","(1721) Ibn Uyaynah narrated to us, on the authority of Amr, on the authority of Abu Al-Sha’tha’i, who said: When you urinate, wipe your penis from below. It will be cut off."
"1722","(1722) Waki’ narrated to us, on the authority of Zam’a bin Salih, on the authority of Isa bin Yazdad, on the authority of his father, that he said: The Messenger of God said God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: When one of you urinates, let him urinate three times. Zam’a said: That will suffice for it."
"1723","(1723) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hamza al-Zayat, on the authority of Ata’ ibn al-Sa’ib, on the authority of Zazan, on the authority of Ali: In the mouse it falls in The well, he said: to be drained until the water overwhelms them."
"1724","(1724) Hafs told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He saw a mouse falling into a well. He said: Forty buckets of water are drawn from it."
"1725","(1725) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; About a rat or cat falling into the well. He said: They lower forty buckets from it. Mughiry said: Until the water changes."
"1726","(1726) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Ata’, who said: If a rat falls into a well, twenty buckets of water are drained from it. If it rots, forty buckets are removed. If the sheep falls, forty buckets are removed. If it rots, all of them are removed, or one hundred buckets."
"1727","(1727) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Sabra, on the authority of Al-Sha’abi; He said: Seventy buckets will be dropped from it, meaning: from the chicken."
"1728","(1728) Ali bin Ubaid told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Ata’; He fell into a well and the chickens and their chicks died in it. He said: Draw a bucket from it and perform ablution from it, for if it rots"
"1729","(1729) Al-Muharbi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Shaybani, on the authority of Hammad; Chickens, dogs, and cats fall into the well and die. He said: Thirty or forty buckets are taken out of it."
"1730","(1730) Ubaidullah bin Musa told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Burqan, on the authority of Al-Zuhri; An animal falls into a well. He said: If the taste or smell of the water does not change, then I see nothing wrong with the water. The water and its fragrance are removed from it until the water becomes fragrant."
"1731","(1731) Asbat bin Muhammad narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhayl; About a chicken falling into a well. He said: Forty buckets of water are drawn from it."
"1732","(1732) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Salamah; That Ali was asked about a boy who urinated in the well? He said: You will be displaced."
"1733","(1733) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ata’; An Ethiopian fell into Zamzam and died. He said: So Ibn al-Zubayr ordered that the water of Zamzam be drained. He said: So he made the water not stop. He said: So they looked and saw a spring gushing out from the side of the Black Stone. He said: Then Ibn al-Zubayr said: It is sufficient for you."
"1734","(1734) Abbad bin Al-Awwam told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abi Aroub, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; A Negro fell into Zamzam and died. He said: Then a man came down to him and took him out, then he said: Bleed out all the water in it, then he said For the one in the well: Place your bucket in front of the spring next to the house, or the corner, for they are from the eyes of the jinn."
"1735","(1735) Abd al-A’la ibn Abd al-A’la narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Ishaq, on the authority of al-Zuhri, on the authority of Urwah, on the authority of Zaid ibn Khaled Al-Jahni said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever touches his private parts, let him perform ablution.\n(Ahmad 5/194. Tabarani 5222)"
"1736","(1736) Mu’alla bin Mansour narrated to us, saying: Al-Haytham bin Humaid narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Ala’ bin Al-Harith, on the authority of Makhoul, on the authority of Anbassa bin Abi Sufyan, on the authority of Umm Habiba, she said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever touches his private parts Let him perform ablution. (Ibn Majah 481)"
"1737","(1737) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Abi Bakr, who said: I heard Urwah bin Al-Zubair speaking to my father, He said: Marwan reminded me of touching the penis, so I said: There is no ablution in it. He said: The secret of his son Safwan was used in it. So he sent a messenger to her and mentioned that she had spoken, and that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Whoever touches his penis Let him perform ablution.\n(Abu Dawud 183. Tirmidhi 83)"
"1738","(1738) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Salamah ibn Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I asked `Ubaydah about the Almighty’s saying: {or Have you touched women? He said: With his hand, so I thought what he meant so I did not ask him. He said: I was informed that whenever Ibn Umar touched his private parts, he would perform ablution. Muhammad said: So I thought that Ibn Omar’s statement and Ubaidah’s statement were the same thing."
"1739","(1739) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Yazid al-Rashk, who said: I heard Jabir ibn Zayd saying: When he touched him He deliberately repeated the ablution."
"1740","(1740) Mu’tamir narrated to us, on the authority of Burd, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: If he touches his penis, he performs ablution."
"1741","(1741) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, that he heard Sa`id bin al-Musayyab say: Whoever touches He mentioned it, so performing ablution on it is obligatory."
"1742","(1742) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Abi Khalid, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Mus’ab bin Sa’d, he said: I was He held the Qur’an to my father, and I put my hand in this way, meaning: he touched his penis, and he said to him: Perform ablution."
"1743","(1743) Ismail Ibn Aliyya told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Nafi’; Ibn Umar prayed one day after Dhuha, and he said: I touched my penis and forgot it."
"1744","(1744) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Nafi’; If Ibn Umar touched his private parts, he would repeat his ablution."
"1745","(1745) Yahya bin Abi Bukair told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, who said: I heard Ibn Abi Najih mention, He said: Ata’ and Mujahid said: Whoever touches his penis, let him perform ablution."
"1746","(1746) Maan bin Issa told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Abdullah bin Akhi Al-Zuhri, who said: I heard Al-Zuhri say: Whoever touches He mentioned it and performed ablution."
"1747","(1747) His youth narrated to us, he said: Shu’bah narrated to us, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, and Ibn Umar, they said: Who touched He mentioned it and performed ablution."
"1748","(1748) Ghandar told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Khudair, who said: Tawoos was asked about touching the penis or the man during prayer? He said: Ugh, ugh, and why did he touch it? He performs ablution."
"1749","(1749) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qais, on the authority of Huzayl; That his brother Arqam bin Shurahbil asked Ibn Masoud, and he said: I have intercourse with you and should I put my hands toward my private parts? Ibn Masoud said: If you know that some of your semen is impure, cut it off."
"1750","(1750) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, who said: A man asked Sa’d about touching the penis? He said: If you know that some part of you is impure, cut it off."
"1751","(1751) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Hudhayfah Ibn Al-Yaman, he said: I don’t care if you touch my penis or my ears."
"1752","(1752) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Qais bin Sakan, who said: Abdullah said: I don’t care. I touched my penis, my thumb, my ears, or my nose."
"1753","(1753) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Minhal, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, similar to him."
"1754","(1754) Ibn Fudayl and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Umair bin Sa’id, who said: I was sitting in a gathering. There is Ammar bin Yasser, so he was asked about touching the penis during prayer? He said: It is only a small portion of yours, and there is another place other than it that is sufficient for you."
"1755","(1755) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Humaid, on the authority of Al-Hasan; Imran bin Husayn said: I don’t care if I touch him, or the inside of my thigh, meaning: he remembers him."
"1756","(1756) Mulazim bin Amr told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Badr, on the authority of Qays bin Talq, on the authority of his father Talq bin Ali, who said: We went out as a delegation until we came to the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, and we pledged allegiance to him and we prayed with him. Then a man came and said: O Messenger of God, what do you think about touching the penis during prayer? He said: Is it anything but a small amount, or a chewable portion of your blood?\n(Abu Dawud 184. Tirmidhi 85)"
"1757","(1757) Jarir told us, on the authority of Qaboos, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali was asked about a man who touches his penis? He said: No problem."
"1758","(1758) Abdul-Wahhab Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Uthman bin Khathim, on the authority of Saeed bin Jubayr, who said: I asked him about touching the penis during prayer? He said: I don't care whether I touched him or denied it."
"1759","(1759) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: There is no harm for a man to touch his penis during prayer."
"1760","(1760) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abu Hamza, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Hudhayfy said: I don’t care if I touch him, or I touched my nose, and Ali said: I don’t care whether I touch him or the tip of my ears."
"1761","(1761) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Abi Najih, who said: Tawoos said And Saeed bin Jubayr: Whoever touches his penis without wanting to, does not have to perform ablution."
"1762","(1762) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ja’far bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Al-Qasim, on the authority of Abu Umamah; That the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was asked about touching the penis? He said: It is nothing but an example from you. (Abdul Razzaq 425. Ibn Majah 484)"
"1763","(1763) Hussein bin Ali told us, he said: Zaid told us, on the authority of Ibrahim bin Muhajir, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Alqamiya. , on the authority of Abdullah; He was asked about touching the penis? He said: There is no harm in it."
"1764","(1764) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Shu’bah, he said: I asked the ruling about a man who performed his ritual urination and his urination occurred during his ritual ablution? He said: He took it like this and threw it out, and Shu'bah said: He scoops it out of the vessel with his hand. So he throws it away."
"1765","(1765) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; In the marrow, he said: Take it and take what it carried, for if there are slugs in it, it has spoiled the bird or the water."
"1766","(1766) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Rabi’, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the pituitary gland, it falls into the water. He said: Throw it in and perform ablution."
"1767","(1767) Mu`tamar narrated to us, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Touching with the hand."
"1768","(1768) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It is intercourse."
"1769","(1769) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Dawud, on the authority of Ja`far bin Iyas, on the authority of Sa`id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, the same."
"1770","(1770) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, on the authority of Abdullah’s companions, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: Touching is short of intercourse."
"1771","(1771) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Ash-Sha’bi, on the authority of Ali’s companions, on the authority of Ali: {or have you touched women} He said: Intercourse"
"1772","(1772) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Intercourse"
"1773","(1773) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abdullah, who said: Nothing less than intercourse."
"1774","(1774) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Salamah ibn Alqamiya, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I asked `Ubaydah about the Almighty’s saying: {or You have touched women. He said: With his hand. I thought what he meant, so I did not ask him."
"1775","(1775) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan bin Saleh, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Hilal bin Yassaf, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, who said: What is less than intercourse?"
"1776","(1776) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: I asked Ubaydah about the Almighty’s saying: {Or have you touched women?} He said: With his hand like this, and he closed his palm."
"1777","(1777) Abdul-Ala told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan, he said[corrupt] : Touching during sexual intercourse."
"1778","(1778) Ali bin Musahir told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Touching is something short of intercourse."
"1779","(1779) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Misra, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, who said: I and some Arabs disagreed about touching, so I and some people from the progeny said: Touching is short of intercourse, and the Arabs said: It is intercourse. So we came to Ibn Abbas, and he said: The Arabs have prevailed, and that is the group."
"1780","(1780) Ibn Fudail narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Ubaidah, on the authority of Abdullah, he said: The Qiblah Of touching, it includes ablution, and touching does not include intercourse."
"1781","(1781) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Abu Bishr, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: Touching and being touched And direct intercourse, but God grants me whatever He wills for whatever He wills."
"1782","(1782) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Tawus; A drop of wine fell into water? His thoughts"
"1783","(1783) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In love) do you drip drops of wine or blood into it? He said: Hiraq."
"1784",""
"1785","(1785) Hammad bin Masadi told us, on the authority of Yazid, the client of Salamah; That Salamah was dripping between his skin and clothes."
"1786",""
"1787",""
"1788","(1788) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, on the authority of a servant of Ibn Azhar, who said: I complained to Ibn Umar al-Bul, He said: If she performs ablution and he wipes it off, then it is from Satan."
"1789","(1789) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Dhib, he said: My brother informed me, he said: I asked Al-Qasim about the calamity and I found it. In prayer? He said: O son of your brother, cleanse him and his father for him, for he is from Satan. He said: So I did so and he went away from him."
"1790","(1790) Khalid bin Hayyan told us, on the authority of Jafar, who said: A man came to Maimun bin Mihran and complained to him about a calamity. He found her, and Maimun said to him: If you perform ablution, sprinkle your private parts and whatever part of your garment is covered with water. That is something, so say: It is from that."
"1791","(1791) Muhammad bin Abi Adi told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Muhammad; When he performed ablution and finished, he would say: With a handful of water in his garment, like this."
"1792","(1792) Muhammad bin Bishr told us, he said: Zakaria bin Abi Zayed told us, he said: Mansour said: Mujahid told me, On the authority of Al-Hakam bin Sufyan Al-Thaqafi: He saw the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, perform ablution, then take a handful of water and sprinkle it on his private parts.\n(Abu Dawud 1688 and Ahmad 409)"
"1793","(1793) Al-Hasan bin Musa told us, he said: Ibn Lahia told us, on the authority of Aqil, on the authority of Ibn Shihab, on the authority of Urwa, on the authority of Asama bin Zaid bin Harithah, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution, then took a handful of water and sprinkled his private parts with it.\n(Ahmad 161, Ibn Majah 492)"
"1794","(1794) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayf ibn al-Yaman, who said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was May God bless him and grant him peace. When he gets up and finds someone fresh, use the siwak. (Bukhari 1136, Muslim 46)"
"1795","(1795) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhayfah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, The same, except that he did not use the siwak. (Muslim 220)"
"1796","(1796) Sharik narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Miqdam ibn Shurayh, on the authority of his father, he said: I asked Aisha, I said: Tell me what. Something that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to say when he entered upon you? She said: He used to start with the siwak. \n(Muslim 220, Abu Dawud 52)"
"1797","(1797) Ali bin Ubaid narrated to us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Muhammad bin Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Abd The Most Gracious, on the authority of Zayd bin Khalid Al-Janni, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: Were it not that I would make it difficult for his nation I would have commanded them to use the siwak for every prayer. He said: Zayd bin Khalid had a siwak on his ears, where a pen is on the ear. The writer, so he does not stand up to pray unless he straightens, then returns it to its place. (Abu Dawud 48. Tirmidhi 23)"
"1798","(1798) Abu Asama and Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Ubaid Allah ibn Umar, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Abi Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Hariri, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: Were it not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have ordered them to use the siwak before everyone. Ablution\n(Ahmad 2/433. An-Nasa’i 3037)"
"1799","(1799) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar narrated to us, on the authority of Haram bin Uthman, on the authority of Abu Atiq, on the authority of Jabir, who said: He used to be quiet when He took his bed, and when he got up during the night, and when he went out in the morning, he said: So I said to him: You have made yourself difficult with this. The siwak? He said: Osama told me that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to use this siwak."
"1800","(1800) Uthman bin Ali told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Habib, on the authority of Sa’id bin Jubayr, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: It was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed two rak’ahs, then he remained silent. (Ahmad 1/218, An-Nasa’i 405)"
"1801","(1801) Hussein bin Ali told us, on the authority of Zayed, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Hudhayfah; When the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would get up at night, he would use a siwak."
"1802","(1802) Affan told us, he said: Hammam told us, he said: Ali ibn Zayd ibn Jud’an told me, he said Umm Muhammad told me, On the authority of Aisha; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would not sleep during the day or night and wake up unless he dressed himself before he He performs ablution.\n(Ibn Saad 483. Ahmad 6/121)"
"1803","(1803) Khalid bin Mukhlid told us, he said: Ibrahim bin Ismail bin Abi Habib told us, he said: Dawud bin Al-Husayn, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: The siwak is a purifier. For the mouth, pleasing to the Lord. (Ahmad 6/146, Darami 684)"
"1804","(1804) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Tamimi, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: We were commanded to use the siwak. We even thought that it would descend therein. (Tayalisi 2739)"
"1805","(1805) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Asama bin Zaid, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan; His servants ibn al-Samit and the companions of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, used to go with the siwaks on their ears."
"1806","(1806) Muawiyah bin Hisham narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Qurum narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Habib, on the authority of a man from the people of Al-Hijaz, on the authority of Abdullah bin Al-Zubayr, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, who said: Were it not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would command them. Using the siwak at every prayer. (Tabarani in Al-Kabir 325)"
"1807","(1807) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, he said: Mis’ar narrated to us, he said: Muhammad bin Jahadi narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, he said: Al-Siwak A purifier for the mouth and a cleanser for the eyes."
"1808","(1808) Ubaidah bin Hamid narrated to us, saying: Al-Amash narrated to us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Yassar, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Abi Layla, on the authority of some of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, who raised him up and said: Were it not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have imposed it on my nation. The siwak, just as purity was enjoined upon them. (Ahmad 5/410; Al-Bazzar 1302)"
"1809","(1809) Abu Khaled Al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Abu Sura, the son of my brother Abi Ayyub, on the authority of Abi Ayyub; The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, would often rest during the night. (Ahmad 5/417)"
"1810","(1810) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, on the authority of Ali, who said: So If one of you gets up during the night, let him wear it. If a man gets up during the night and cleanses himself, then performs ablution, then gets up to pray, he will come to him. Until the king stands behind him and listens to the Qur’an, he continues to approach it until he places his mouth on it, but it does not recite. Oh, but it entered his stomach. (Bazzar 603)"
"1811","(1811) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Al-Hakam, he said: This revelation was revealed to Mujahid, and he was the most persistent in his behavior. The siwak"
"1812","(1812) Kathir ibn Hisham narrated to us, on the authority of Ja’far ibn Burqan, he said: Yazeed ibn al-Asam narrated to us, he said: It was a siwak Maimunah Ibn Al-Harith, the wife of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, is soaked in water. If work or prayer distracts him from it, Otherwise, she would take it and remain silent."
"1813","(1813) Zayd bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hajjaj, on the authority of Makhoul, who said: Abu Ayyub said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said Peace and blessings of God be upon him: Four of the Sunnahs of the Messengers: wearing perfume, getting married, using the siwak, and henna. \n(Tirmidhi 1080, Ahmad 5/421)"
"1814","(1814) Waki’ told us, he said: Abd al-Rahman bin Amr al-Awza’i told us, on the authority of Hassan bin Atiyya, he said: Ablution Half of faith, and the siwak is half of ablution, and were it not that I would make it difficult for my nation, I would have ordered them to use the siwak at every prayer. Two rak'ahs in which a servant can rest in peace is better than seventy rak'ahs in which he does not rest in peace."
"1815","(1815) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Dinar, on the authority of Ibn Umar, he said: Because I received Of my affairs, I have not managed, meaning: in the siwak, more beloved to me than two servants. He said: Ibn Umar would not eat food except Astanna, meaning: Astana."
"1816","(1816) Waki’ told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, he said: I heard Mujahid, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, was slow. He greeted Gabriel and said: How will we come to you when you do not cut your nails, do not polish your knuckles, and do not be quiet?"
"1817","(1817) Waki` narrated to us, he said: Sufyan narrated to us, on the authority of Musa bin Abi Aisha, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Saad, he said: The Messenger of God said: God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him: Be calm, clean yourself, and perform the Witr prayer, for God is a Witr prayer and loves the Witr prayer."
"1818","(1818) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Mundhir ibn Tha’labiyah Al-Abdi, on the authority of Abdullah ibn Buraida Al-Aslami, who said: Whenever the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, woke up from his family, he would call his maid and it would be said to her: “Perfect with the siwak.”"
"1819","(1819) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Mis`ar, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Jahadi, on the authority of al-Sha`bi, who said: The siwak is a cleanser for the eyes. For the mouth"
"1820","(1820) Waki’ told us, he said: Israel told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Tamimi, he said: I asked Ibn Abbas about the siwak? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, did not stop enjoining it to the point that we thought that it would come down to him."
"1821","(1821) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Salih bin Kaysan, who said: The man was one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God’s peace and blessings be upon him and the siwak on his ears."
"1822","(1822) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abdul-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Shuaib, on the authority of Anas, he said: The Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, said: And peace be upon him: I have increased your use of the siwak. (Bukhari 888, Ahmad 3/143)"
"1823","(1823) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughiriya, on the authority of a servant of Al-Hayy, who said: Abu Ubaidah used to rest after the Witr prayer. Before the two rak'ahs."
"1824","(1824) Jarir told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, he said: I asked Ibrahim about the siwak? He said: Who can tolerate the siwak? They used to rest after the Witr prayer and before the two rak'ahs."
"1825","(1825) Abdullah bin Al-Mubarak and Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwa, on the authority of his father; He used to perform the ritual prayer twice, before dawn and before noon."
"1826","(1826) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: Yahya bin Wathhab used to stay in the mosque, so when the prayer was established He prayed and did not touch water."
"1827","(1827) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of Jarir; He used to cleanse you and order them to perform ablution using his siwak."
"1828","(1828) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibrahim; He saw no harm in performing ablution due to the use of the siwak."
"1829","(1829) Mu’tamar bin Sulaiman told us, on the authority of Sallam bin Abi Dhiyal, on the authority of Al-Hasan; When a woman sees her dress stained with milk, should she pray and not wash her dress? He said: There is nothing impure in her milk."
"1830","(1830) Malik bin Ismail told us, he said: Ja’far al-Ahmar told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: There is no harm in milk. A woman’s dream is that her dress is stained, meaning: her milk."
"1831","(1831) Hafs bin Ghayath told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: A man from Ibn Abbas stood up and said to him: Where? He said: Spill water. He said: Do not say: Spill, but say: I urinate."
"1832","(1832) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Misra, on the authority of Al-Azraq ibn Qais, that he heard Ibn Umar; He hated to say: I stand up and shed water."
"1833","(1833) Khaled bin Mukhlid narrated to us, saying: Suleiman bin Bilal narrated to us, on the authority of Suhail bin Abi Saleh, on the authority of his father, that Omar said to a man: Do not say: I shed water, but say: I urinate."
"1834","(1834) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Qais, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ahwas, on the authority of Abdullah; He hated to say: I will spill the water."
"1835","(1835) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hamid, on the authority of Bakr, on the authority of Abu Rafi’, on the authority of Abu Hurairah; He met the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, on one of the roads of Medina while he was in a state of ritual impurity, so he slipped away and went and took a bath. So the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, lost him, and when he came to him, he said: Where have you been, Abu Hurairah? He said: O Messenger of God, you met me while I was in a state of ritual impurity, and I thought I would sit with you until I took a bath. He said: Glory be to God, the believer does not It defiles you. (Bukhari 285. Abu Dawud 234)"
"1836","(1836) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Mis’ar, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, met him while he was junub, so he turned away from him and took a bath, then he came and said: The believer does not It defiles you. (Abu Dawud 233. An-Nasa’i 264)"
"1837","(1837) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, who said: I was informed that the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace Hudhayfah saw Faragh and said: Did I not see you? He said: Yes, O Messenger of God, but I was in a state of ritual impurity, so he said: A believer does not become impure."
"1838","(1838) Muhammad bin Bishr narrated to us, saying: Zakaria bin Abi Zayed narrated to us, saying: I heard Amir mentioning on the authority of Ibn Abbas. He said: He does not avoid water, nor clothing, nor earth, nor man."
"1839","(1839) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Abu Razin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, he said: I heard the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. He says: If a dog licks the vessel of one of you, let him wash it seven times. (Muslim 89. An-Nasa’i 65)"
"1840","(1840) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Abu Hurairah, on the authority of the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him. He, peace and blessings of God be upon him, said: To purify the vessel of one of you if a dog licks it, to wash it seven times, and fill it with dirt. \n(Muslim 234. Ahmad 2/427)"
"1841","(1841) Hammad bin Khaled told us, on the authority of Al-Amri, on the authority of Nafi’, on the authority of Ibn Omar; If a dog licks a vessel, it should be washed seven times."
"1842","(1842) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Harmala, on the authority of Ibn al-Musayyab, who said: Wash your vessels seven times."
"1843","(1843) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; About the dog licking the vessel. He said: Wash it until you clean it."
"1844","(1844) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mughiryah, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Wash it until you purify it."
"1845","(1845) Shababah ibn Siwar narrated to us, he said: Shu’ba narrated to us, on the authority of Abu al-Tayyah, he said: I heard Mutarrif narrating on the authority of Ibn What is overlooked is that the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If a dog licks a vessel, wash it seven times and wipe it clean. Eighth: With dust. (Abu Dawud 75. An-Nasa’i 70)"
"1846","(1846) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan; In the rain mud gets on the garment. He said: If he wants, he can wash it, or if he wants, leave it until it dries, then rub it."
"1847","(1847) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Mansour, who said: I asked Mujahid about rain mud getting on the clothes? He said: When it gets dry, it is wet."
"1848","(1848) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Hajjaj ibn Dinar, who said: I asked Abu Ja`far about rain mud getting on my clothes? He said: The good land makes good the bad land."
"1849","(1849) Yahya bin Saeed told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Ubaid bin Umair had two characteristics. When he performed ablution, he would wipe over them."
"1850","(1850) Abdul Salam told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Which parts of your head did you wipe over?"
"1851","(1851) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ismail Al-Azraq, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Which parts of your head did you wipe over?"
"1852","(1852) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ibn Juraij, on the authority of Ata’, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wiped the front of his head."
"1853","(1853) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Khalid Al-Hadha’, who said, “It has informed me that Ibn Umar used to say: Enough water.” Thus, he described that he dipped them in water, then wiped his head in this manner. He placed his palms in the middle of his head, then brought them to the front of his head."
"1854","(1854) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, he said: I asked Ibn Sirin about a man who urinates in his house while he is praying. What is it? He thought of it, and I asked Al-Hasan, and he said: Yes, and he will not abandon it."
"1855","(1855) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Bakr bin Ma’iz, on the authority of Ibn Buraidah He counts it on the authority of his father. He said: Do not urinate in a basin in a house in which you pray, and do not urinate in your bathing place."
"1856","(1856) Ibn Fudail told us, on the authority of Abu Sinan, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Angels do not enter a house in which Urine"
"1857","(1857) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ubaid bin Abi Al-Wasim, on the authority of Salman Abi Shaddad, who said: It was Abu Rafi’ My master of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered me to hand him the urinal while he was on his bed and he would urinate in it."
"1858","(1858) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abu Awan narrated to us, he said: Sa’id bin Abi Barda narrated to us, he said: I saw Abu Wael He was sitting in the mosque of the House, then he called for a basin and urinated in it."
"1859","(1859) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Shu’abi, he said: I asked Al-Hakam about washing and performing ablution with snow? He said: He should break it, wash himself, and perform ablution."
"1860","(1860) Waki’ told us, he said: Sufyan told us, on the authority of Jabir, on the authority of Amer, and Al-Hakam, who said: There is no harm in performing ablution in the snow."
"1861","(1861) Hafs told us, on the authority of a sheikh, who said: Salem used to perform tayammum when the water was solid."
"1862","(1862) Waki` narrated to us, saying: Sufyan used to treat it well, and he would wash from it and perform ablution."
"1863","(1863) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath bin Abdul-Malik, on the authority of Al-Hasan; He was asked about a man who took a bath with snow and was struck by cold and died? He said: What a witness she has."
"1864","(1864) Hushaym bin Bashir told us, saying: Dawud bin Amr told us, on the authority of Busr bin Ubaid Allah Al-Hadrami, on the authority of Abu Idris Al-Khawlani, he said: Awf bin Malik Al-Ashja’i told us; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, ordered wiping over the socks during the campaign against Tabuk. Three days and two nights for the traveler, and one day and night for the resident.\n(Ahmad 6/27 Daraqutni 18)"
"1865","(1865) Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour told us, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, on the authority of Aflah the client of Abu Ayyub, on the authority of Abi Ayyub; He was commanded to wipe over the socks, and he was washing his feet, and he was told about that: How? Do you order wiping while washing? He said: How miserable is my condition if it is a haven for you and a sin against me. I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. He does it and commands it, but I love ablution. (Ahmad 5/421)"
"1866","(1866) Hushaym told us, he said: Al-A’mash told us, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Hudhayfah, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace. May God bless him and grant him peace. The captives of a people came and urinated on them, so I brought water to him and he performed ablution and wiped over his socks. (Abu Dawud 24. Tirmidhi 13)"
"1867","(1867) Hushaym told us, he said, Husayn told us, on the authority of Salim bin Abi al-Ja’d, and on the authority of Abu Sufyan, that they heard Al-Mugheerah ibn Shu’ba narrates, he said: I was with the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on a journey, and he came out for his need, and when When he finished, I brought him a bowl containing water, so he poured it on him, and he was wearing a narrow robe with two sleeves. He said: So he came out. He took his hand from under his forehead, washed his arms, and wiped his socks. (Bukhari 1820, Muslim 269)"
"1868","(1868) Abu Muawiyah and Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam, who said: By Jarir bin Abd God, and he performed ablution and wiped over his socks, and it was said to him: Will you do this? He said: What prevents me when I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing it? Ibrahim said: We liked the hadith of Jarir because he converted to Islam after the revelation of the Prophet.\n(Bukhari 387. Muslim 227)"
"1869","(1869) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, on the authority of Muawiyah ibn Salih, he said: Damra ibn Habib narrated to us, on the authority of Jarir ibn Abd. God said: I came to the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, after the revelation of Surah Al-Ma’idah, and I saw him wiping over him. The hidden ones\n(Daraqutni 193)"
"1870","(1870) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Muslim, on the authority of Masruq, on the authority of Al-Mughirah ibn Shu’bah, he said: I was with The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey, and he said: O Mughirah, take the medicine. He said: So I took it and then went out with him. Then the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, set off until he disappeared and fulfilled his need, then he came wearing a Syrian robe. The sleeves became narrow, so he went to take his hand out of the sleeves, and they became narrow, so he took his hand out from underneath them. So I poured water on him, and he performed ablution as he does for prayer, then he wiped over his socks and prayed."
"1871","(1871) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ka’b ibn Ajra, on the authority of Bilal; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped over the socks and the veil."
"1872","(1872) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Alqamiya bin Marthad, on the authority of Sulaiman bin Buraidah, on the authority of his father; On the day of the conquest of Mecca, the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, performed ablution and wiped over his socks, and Omar said to him: O Messenger of God, I saw you doing something today that you would not have done before today, so he said: O Omar, I did it intentionally.\n(Abu Dawud 174. Tirmidhi 61)"
"1873","(1873) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Dulham bin Salih, on the authority of Hujar bin Abdullah al-Kindi, on the authority of Ibn Buraydah, on the authority of His father; Al-Najashi presented two simple black slippers to the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, and he put them on and then performed ablution. And he wiped over them. (Abu Dawud 1560, Tirmidhi 2820)"
"1874","(1874) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham Al-Dastawai, who said: Hammad narrated to us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jadali, on the authority of Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, that the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, used to say: A traveler’s anointing is required for three times. And for the resident there is a day and a night. (Abu Dawud 158. Tabarani 3763)"
"1875","(1875) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Abu Abdullah Al-Jadali, on the authority of Khuzaymah bin Thabit said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, made the traveler wipe three times, and if we had asked for more, we would have increased.\n(Tabarani 3756)"
"1876","(1876) Al-Fadl bin Dukain narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, on the authority of Amr bin Maymun. On the authority of Abu Abdullah al-Jadali, on the authority of Khuzaymah ibn Thabit, who said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, placed the wiping cloth on him. The socks are three days for the traveler, and one day for the resident, and if the questioner had continued with his question, he would have made it five days. (Tirmidhi 95. Abu Dawud 158)"
"1877","(1877) Zaid bin Harun told us, saying: Hajjaj bin Arta told us, on the authority of Yahya bin Ubad Al-Birani, On the authority of Muhammad bin Saad, he said: He used to perform ablution in the corner, and one day some stool came out on us, so he performed ablution and wiped over it. It was hidden, so we were amazed and said: What is this? He said: My father told me that he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, doing the same as I did.\n(Ahmad 1/186)"
"1878","(1878) Abu Muawiyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymara, on the authority of Shurayh bin Hani’ Al-Harithi, who said: I asked Aisha about wiping, and she said: Go to Ali, for he knows that better than me, so ask him. So I went to Ali and asked him about Scanning? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, commanded us to wipe the resident one day and one night, and the traveler three days. (Muslim 232. Ahmad 1/113)"
"1879","(1879) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Dhar, who said: I came to Safwan bin Assal Al-Muradi, and he said: What brings you? I said: seeking knowledge. He said: For the angels spread their wings for the seeker of knowledge.\n He said: Whenever the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was on a journey, he commanded us not to remove our socks for three days, except From sexual impurity, but also from defecation, urination, and sleep. (Tirmidhi 3535. Ahmad 4/239)"
"1880","(1880) Affan told us, he said: Hammad bin Salamah told us, he said: Ayoub told us, on the authority of Abu Qalabab, on the authority of Abu Idris, On the authority of Bilal, he said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, wiping over those who were standing and wearing the veil. \n(Ibn Khuzaymah 1891, Ahmad 15)"
"1881","(1881) Yunus told us, on the authority of Dawud ibn Abi al-Furat, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Zayd, on the authority of Abu Shurayh, on the authority of Abu Muslim My servant Zaid bin Suhan, he said: I was with Salman, and he saw a man taking off his socks to perform ablution, and Salman said to him: Wipe. On your socks and on your veil and wipe with your forelocks, for I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiping on The socks and the veil."
"1882","(1882) Yahya bin Ishaq narrated to us, saying: Yahya bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Razin, on the authority of Muhammad Bin Yazid bin Abi Ziyad, on the authority of Ayoub bin Qattan Al-Kindi, on the authority of Ubayy bin Amara Al-Ansari, he said: And it was The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, prayed in his house facing the two qiblahs. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, wipe over The socks? He said: Yes, he said: I said: O Messenger of God, what day? He said: Yes, and two days. I said: O Messenger of God, two days? He said: Yes, and three. He said: I said: O Messenger of God, and three? He said: Yes, and whatever you want. (Abu Dawud 1591, Tabarani 545)"
"1883","(1883) Ibn Uyaynah told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Muhammad, on the authority of Hamza bin Al-Mughirah, on the authority of his father; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, fulfilled his need, then he came and performed ablution, wiped his head, and wiped over his socks.\n(Muslim 318 and Abd al-Razzaq 749)"
"1884","(1884) Zaid bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Khaled bin Abi Bakr, Salim bin Abdullah told me, on the authority of his father; That Omar bin Al-Khattab asked him Saad bin Abi Waqqas about wiping over the socks? Omar said: I heard the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, ordering wiping over the socks when one wears them while they are pure. (Abu Ali 171)"
"1885","(1885) Al-Fadl bin Dukain and Yahya bin Adam narrated to us, on the authority of Hassan bin Salih, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Salem, on the authority of Ibn Omar, on the authority of Omar, said: I saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiping his socks with water while travelling.\n(Ahmad 1/54)"
"1886","(1886) Muawiyah bin Hisham told us, on the authority of Shayban, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, that Jafar bin Amr bin Umayyah told him that his father told him that he saw the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, anointing On the socks.\n(Bukhari 204. Ahmad 5/288)"
"1887","(1887) Muhammad bin Musab narrated to us, saying: Al-Awza’i narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Kathir, on the authority of Abu Salama, on the authority of Jafar bin Amr bin Umayyah, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped over the socks and the turban."
"1888","(1888) Jarir bin Abdul Hamid told us, on the authority of Abdul Aziz bin Rafi’, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’, he said: He addressed us. Al-Mughirah bin Shu’ba, and he said: O people, I was with the Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, on a ride. So he came down and made the final decision. He needed water, so I brought him water and he performed ablution and wiped over his socks."
"1889","(1889) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, on the authority of Muhammad ibn Sirin, on the authority of Amr ibn Wahhab al-Thaqafi, on the authority of al-Mughirah Bin Shu'ba; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, went to reveal his hand, and he was wearing a Levantine robe with narrow sleeves. So he took his hand out from under it, washed his face and hands, then wiped with his forelocks, wiped over the turban, and wiped On the socks."
"1890","(1890) Zayd ibn al-Hubab narrated to us, saying: Abd al-Wahhab narrated to us, saying: Al-Muhajir, the master of the virgins, narrated to us, on the authority of Abd Al-Rahman bin Abi Bakra, on the authority of his father; The Prophet, may God’s prayers and peace be upon him, appointed for a traveler a period of three days and two nights, and for a resident a day and a night."
"1891","(1891) Hushaym told us, he said: Zaid bin Abi Ziyad told us, he said: Zaid bin Wahhab told us, he said: He wrote We refer to Umar ibn al-Khattab regarding wiping over the socks. Three days and two nights for the traveler, and one day and night for the resident."
"1892","(1892) Yazeed bin Harun told us, on the authority of Abu Malik Al-Ashja’i, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Ibn Umar, that Umar bin Al-Khattab said regarding wiping over the socks: For the traveler three days and for the resident one day until the night."
"1893","(1893) Abu Al-Ahwas narrated to us, on the authority of Imran bin Muslim, who said: We said to Nubati Al-Jufi’i, and he was the boldest of us regarding Omar: He asked him about wiping over the socks, so he asked him and said: For the traveler there are three days, and for the resident one day and a night."
"1894","(1894) Waki’ narrated to us, Jarir bin Ayyub narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Zur’i bin Amr, who said: I saw Jarir wiping over me. Hidden, he said: Abu Zur’a said: Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you enters His feet are in his socks and they are pure, so let him wipe over them. Three days for a traveler, and one day for a resident."
"1895","(1895) Hushaym told us, saying: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, that Omar bin Al-Khattab, Saad bin Malik, and Ibn Masoud: They used to wipe over the socks."
"1896","(1896) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mujalid, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: I asked Ibn Umar about wiping over the socks? He said: Wipe over them."
"1897","(1897) Hushaym told us, saying: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Abraham, he said: The Companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped On the socks, so whoever abandons that out of desire, then it is from Satan."
"1898","(1898) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Muharib, on the authority of Ibn Umar, who said: Saad and I disagreed in Al-Qadisiyah. Regarding wiping over the socks, Saad said: Wipe over them, and I denied that. When we came to Omar bin Al-Khattab, he mentioned This was the case of Saad, and he said to him: Did you not see that Ibn Umar denies wiping over the socks? He said: So I said: O Commander of the Faithful, that Sa`d says: Wipe over them after the accident. He said: Then Omar said: Not after the accident, not? After the myths"
"1899","(1899) Hushaym told us, he said: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hakam bin Al-Araj, he said: I asked Ibn Umar about wiping over someone’s body. The socks, and he said: Saad and I disagreed about that, and we were in Jalawla, so Saad said: Wipe over them, so I denied that. When we came to Omar, I mentioned that to him, and he said: O Commander of the Faithful, he says: Wipe over them after the incident. Omar said: Except after the news, except after the event."
"1900","(1900) Hushaym told us, he said: Husayn told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Ibn Masoud, that he used to say in Wiping over the socks: three days and two nights for the traveler, and one day and night for the resident."
"1901","(1901) Hushaym told us, he said: Ghailan bin Abdullah, the client of Banu Makhzum, told us: I heard Ibn Umar, An Ansar man asked him about wiping over the socks. He said: Three days for a traveler, and a day and a night for a resident."
"1902","(1902) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Amr ibn al-Harith, who said: I accompanied Ibn Masoud on a journey. He did not remove his socks three times."
"1903","(1903) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, on the authority of Shaqiq, on the authority of Amr ibn Al-Harith, who said: I went out with Abdullah to Al-Mada’in. So he wiped over his socks three times, without taking them off."
"1904","(1904) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Mukhaymara, on the authority of Shurayh bin Hani’ He said: Ali said: For the traveler there are three nights, and a day and a night for the resident."
"1905","(1905) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Musa bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr bin Ata, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, who said: To the traveler Three, and for the resident there is a day and a night."
"1906","(1906) Hafs told us, on the authority of Abd al-Malik ibn Sila’, on the authority of Abd Khayr; Verily, Ali wiped over the socks."
"1907","(1907) Hafs narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abd Khair, on the authority of Ali, who said: If religion were based on opinion, The soles of the feet would have been better and more deserving of wiping than the outsides of them, but I saw the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiping They are visible"
"1908","(1908) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zubayr bin Adiy, on the authority of Ata’, on the authority of Ibn Abbas; He anointed"
"1909","(1909) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Ishaq, on the authority of Abi Ubaid bin Muhammad bin Ammar, he said: I asked Jabir about Wiping over the socks? He said: Sunnah."
"1910","(1910) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Jariri, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’ bin Al-Shakhir, on the authority of Iyad bin Nadli, he said: We went out with Abu Musa to some gardens, and he took care of something, and I went out to do something, but I came back intending to take off my hair. It was hidden, so he said: Spread them and wipe over them until you put them where you sleep."
"1911","(1911) Abu Dawud al-Talisi told us, on the authority of Shu`bah, on the authority of Simak, he said: I heard Jabir bin Samurah, he said: I would not care if I did not remove my socks three times."
"1912","(1912) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sawada bin Abi Al-Aswad, on the authority of his father, who said: Abdullah bin Amr said: On you. So wear these black slippers, for it is more appropriate for you to wipe over them."
"1913","(1913) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaid Al-Tai, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of a man; That Samura wiped over her socks."
"1914","(1914) Al-Fadl bin Dukayn and Ubaid Allah narrated to us, on the authority of Sa’id bin Ubaid Al-Tai, on the authority of Ali bin Rabi’ah, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Samarra, on the authority of his father; He wiped over the socks."
"1915","(1915) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, and Ibn Aoun, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, he said: I was informed that Abu Ayyub was He ordered his companions to wipe over the socks."
"1916","(1916) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah told us, on the authority of Ibrahim, he said: Jarir bin Abdullah used to wipe over The socks, he said: This was more surprising to me, because Jarir’s conversion to Islam occurred only after the revelation of Al-Ma’idah."
"1917","(1917) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of his brother Isa bin Abdul Rahman, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Omar bin Al-Khattab urinating, performing ablution, and wiping over his socks. He said: I can even see the traces of his fingers on his socks."
"1918","(1918) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Wiping over the socks in a row with the fingers."
"1919","(1919) Abu Al-Ahwas told us, on the authority of Abu Ishaq, on the authority of Abu Al-Ala’, who said: We sent Ali to Siffin, and he used Qays bin Saad, the servant of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, came upon us. We traveled until we came to a dwelling, and I saw Qays with a Then he came to the banks of the Tigris River, performed ablution, and wiped over his socks, and I saw the traces of his fingers on his socks."
"1920","(1920) Abu Muawiyah told us, on the authority of Asim, on the authority of Abu Uthman, who said: Ibn Umar and Saad disagreed regarding wiping over the socks. Saad said: Wipe it."
"1921","(1921) Aidh bin Habib told us, on the authority of Talha bin Yahya, on the authority of Aban bin Uthman, who said: I asked Saad bin Abi Waqqas About wiping over the socks? He said: Yes, three days and two nights for the traveler, and one day and two nights for the resident."
"1922","(1922) Affan narrated to us, he said: Abdul-Warith narrated to us, he said: Ayoub Al-Sakhtiyani narrated to us, on the authority of Yazid bin Mu’naq, on the authority of Mutarrif said: I entered upon Ammar, and I approached him while he was in the open, so he came out, performed ablution, and wiped over his socks."
"1923","(1923) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ibn Abi Arouba, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Musa bin Salamah al-Hudhali, on the authority of Ibn Abbas said: The traveler wipes over his socks for three days and nights, and the resident has a day and night."
"1924","(1924) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ayyub, he said: I saw Al-Hasan at a funeral and he urinated, then he came and performed ablution and wiped over me. Hidden"
"1925","(1925) Ibn Aliyah narrated to us, on the authority of Yahya bin Abi Ishaq, that he heard Anas bin Malik being asked about wiping the body. The socks? He said: Wipe over them, and they said to him: Did you hear it from the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace? He said: No, but I heard it from among our companions who were not orphaned saying: Wiping over the socks, and if he does such-and-such, no. Yes"
"1926","(1926) Hatem bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Abd al-Rahman bin Harmala, who said: Sa`id bin al-Musayyib said: If you enter Your feet are in the socks and they are pure while you are staying. The same is sufficient for you until the next day, and the traveler has three nights."
"1927","(1927) Ali bin Musa al-Jinni told us, on the authority of Amr al-Jamal al-Aswad, who said: I asked about him, “Salim?” He said: “to the traveler.” Three days and three nights, and the resident has one day and one night."
"1928","(1928) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Ali bin Salih, on the authority of Abd al-A’la bin Amir, who said: I saw Ibn al-Hanafiyy wiping over Ali. Hidden"
"1929","(1929) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ubaydah, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: Eight of the companions of the Messenger of God wiped over the socks. May God bless him and grant him peace; Omar bin Al-Khattab, Saad bin Abi Waqqas, Ibn Masoud, Abu Masoud Al-Ansari, Hudhayfah, and Al-Mughirah bin Shu'bah and Al-Bara' bin Aazib."
"1930","(1930) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Bayan, on the authority of Qays, on the authority of a man who said, Bayan: I see him as one of the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace. He, peace and blessings be upon him, said: If I were embarrassed to wipe over my socks, I would be embarrassed to pray in them."
"1931","(1931) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Mughirah. He said: Abraham was on a journey, and a hot day came upon them. He said: Had it not been for Contrary to the Sunnah, I would have removed my socks."
"1932","(1932) Hafs told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I saw Ibrahim urinating, then he performed ablution and wiped over his socks. Then he entered the mosque and prayed."
"1933","(1933) Ibn Fudayl told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Ubaid Allah, he said: I saw Ibrahim Al-Nakha’i, and Ibrahim bin Suwayd, they were new, then they performed ablution and wiped over their socks."
"1934","(1934) Abu Usama told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim Al-Taymi, who said: I asked Al-Harith bin Suwayd about wiping over the body. The socks? He said: Wipe, so I said: Even if I enter the toilet? He said: Even if you enter the private room ten times."
"1935","(1935) Zaid bin Harun told us, he said: Asim told us, he said: I saw Anas bin Malik urinating, then he performed ablution and wiped over me. \nHis turban and slippers"
"1936","(1936) Waki’ told us, he said: Jarir bin Ayyub told us, on the authority of Abu Zur’i bin Amr bin Jarir, he said: I saw Jarir wiped over his socks.\nHe said: Abu Zur’a said: Abu Hurairah said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, said: If one of you inserts his foot In his socks, and they are pure, let him wipe over them; Three days for a traveler, and one day for a resident."
"1937","(1937) Zayd bin Harun told us, he said: Asim told us, he said: I saw a man who had urinated, then he performed ablution and wiped over his turban. And its hiddenness."
"1938","(1938) Ibn Mahdi narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Salama bin Kuhail, on the authority of Ibrahim al-Taymi, on the authority of Al-Harith Ibn Suwayd, on the authority of Abdullah, said: Three days for the traveler, and for the resident, a day and a night. He said: Al-Harith said: I do not take off my socks until I came to my bed."
"1939","(1939) Al-Fadl bin Anas narrated to us, on the authority of Aban bin Abdullah, on the authority of someone who narrated on the authority of Abu Hurairah; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped over the socks. (Ibn Majah 5550, Ibn Hibban 1334)"
"1940","(1940) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Sa’id, who said: I saw Ali bin Rabi’i wiping over his socks and saying: What is in it? I feel some of it."
"1941","(1941) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Shuabi narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Bakr bin Hafs, on the authority of Abi Abdullah, the client of Al-Taym bin Murah, on the authority of Abu Abdul Rahman, who said: I was sitting with Abdul Rahman bin Awf, and he passed by us. Bilal, so we asked him about wiping over the socks? He said: The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, was fulfilling his need and then leaving, so we brought him water and he performed ablution. And He wipes over the men of faith and the turbans. (Abu Dawud 154. Ahmad 6/13)"
"1942","(1942) Yahya bin Ya’li told us, on the authority of Laith, on the authority of Al-Hakam, on the authority of Ibn Abi Layla, on the authority of Ka’b, on the authority of Bilal ; The Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace, Abu Bakr, and Omar used to wipe over the socks and the veil. (Tabarani 1062)"
"1943","(1943) Yahya bin Adam told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan bin Saleh, on the authority of Nasir bin Dhu’luq, on the authority of Ibn Umar; Saad bin Malik wiped over his socks, but Ibn Umar disapproved of that, so he mentioned it to his father and said: Saad bin No one is more knowledgeable than you."
"1944","(1944) Yahya told us, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Saad bin Ubaidah, on the authority of Muhammad bin Yaish al-Bakri, on the authority of Ibn Omar, a man came to him and said: Wipe? Abdullah said: I will go in and then go out and wipe over my socks."
"1945","(1945) Abu Bakr al-Hanafi told us, on the authority of Usama bin Zayd, on the authority of Ishaq, the client of Zaydah; Saad bin Abi Waqqas went out of the toilet and performed ablution and wiped over his socks, and he was told: Should you wipe over them when you had left the toilet? The emptiness? He said: Yes, when you put your slippers on your feet and they are pure, wipe them over them, and do not take them off except for the sake of ritual impurity."
"1946","(1946) Hushaym told us, saying: Mansour and Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say about wiping over The socks: Wipe over them, and do not set aside time for that unless you are in a state of ritual impurity."
"1947","(1947) Zaid bin Harun told us, on the authority of Muhammad bin Amr, on the authority of Abu Salama; He did not take a long time when wiping, and would say: Wipe as long as you want."
"1948","(1948) Othham bin Ali told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Urwah, on the authority of his father; He did not take the time to wipe."
"1949","(1949) Hammad bin Khalid told us, on the authority of Muawiyah bin Salih, on the authority of Iyad bin Abdullah Al-Qurashi, on the authority of Zaid bin Abi Habib; That Abu Ubaidah bin Al-Jarrah sent Uqba bin Amir Al-Janni to Omar bin Al-Khattab about the conquest of Damascus, and he left on the day Friday, and the day of Friday came, so Omar asked him: When did you go out? So he told him, and said: I have not taken off my slippers since I left. Omar said: You have done well."
"1950","(1950) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Hafs, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: They asked him about wiping over the socks? He said: Thus, and directed his hand downward."
"1951","(1951) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Yunus, on the authority of Al-Hasan (h), and Mughirah, on the authority of Ibrahim; They both said about wiping over the socks: Thus, and they described wiping above their fingers."
"1952","(1952) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He wiped them from the outside of his feet to the tips of his fingers."
"1953","(1953) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Shu’bi, who said: Wiping over the socks is like this, and he commanded his hand. From the backs of his feet to the tips of his ankles"
"1954","(1954) Fudayl bin Iyad narrated to us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: Wiping over the socks is done in a row with the fingers."
"1955","(1955) Mukhlid bin Zayd narrated to us, and he was trustworthy, on the authority of Sa’id bin Abdul Aziz, who said: I asked Al-Zuhri about Wiping over the socks? So he said with his hand like this, and passed his fingers from the front of his foot to the top of it."
"1956","(1956) Hushaym told us, he said: I am Yahya bin Saeed, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Muhammad, on the authority of Aisha, she said: Because It is more beloved to me to cut them with knives than to wipe them."
"1957","(1957) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Salem, who said: Mujahid and his companions went out, among them was Abdou bin Abi Lubabah, he said: They went out as pilgrims, and his servant was leading them in prayer. He said: So he came out one day because of his need, but he delayed. Upon them, when he came, Mujahid said to him: What kept you imprisoned? He said: I just fulfilled my need, then I performed ablution and wiped over my socks, so Mujahid said to him: Go ahead and lead us, I don’t know what happened. According to your prayers."
"1958","(1958) Hatim bin Ismail told us, on the authority of Ja’far, on the authority of his father, he said: Ali said: The Book preceded the hidden ones."
"1959","(1959) Ali bin Mushir told us, on the authority of Uthman bin Hakim, on the authority of Ikrimah, on the authority of Ibn Abbas, he said: The book preceded The hidden ones"
"1960","(1960) Ibn Aliyah told us, on the authority of Ruh Ibn al-Qasim, on the authority of Ibn Tawus, on the authority of his father, he said: Ibn Abbas said: If They said that during travel and extreme cold."
"1961","(1961) Ibn Fudayl narrated to us, on the authority of Dirar ibn Murra, on the authority of Sa’id ibn Jubayr, he said: Ibn Abbas said: I don’t care. I wiped over the socks, or I wiped over the backs of my cheeks."
"1962","(1962) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Al-Qasim bin Abi Ayyub, who said: Sa’id bin Jubayr saw me wiping over my socks. Abyadin, he said: So he said to me: Don’t spoil your socks."
"1963","(1963) Ibn Idris told us, on the authority of Fitr, he said: I said to Ata’: Indeed, Ikrimah, he says: Ibn Abbas said: The book preceded The socks. Ata’ said: Ikrimah lied. I saw Ibn Abbas wiping over them."
"1964","(1964) Yunus bin Muhammad told us, he said: Abd al-Wahid bin Ziyad told us, he said: Ismail bin Sami’ told us, he said: Abu Razin told me, he said: Abu Hurairah said: I don’t care whether I wipe over the back of a shoe, or whether I wipe over the back of a donkey."
"1965","(1965) Yahya bin Abi Bukair narrated to us, saying: Shuabi narrated to us, on the authority of Abi Bakr bin Hafs, he said: I heard Urwa bin Al-Zubair, on the authority of Aisha, said: Because I slit them, or cut my fingers with a knife, is more beloved to me than wiping them. On them."
"1966","(1966) Jarir narrated to us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: Wiping over the socks is bitter."
"1967","(1967) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Al-Hasan, who said: He wipes over the socks once."
"1968","(1968) Abdul Rahim bin Suleiman told us, on the authority of Suleiman, he said: I saw Abraham, he performed ablution and wiped over his socks. One"
"1969","(1969) Al-Hanafi narrated to us, on the authority of Abu Amir Al-Khazzaz, he said: Al-Hasan narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Mughirah bin Shu’abi, he said: I saw The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, urinated, then came and performed ablution, wiped over his socks, and placed his right hand on them. His right sock, and his left hand was on his left sock, then he wiped over the tops of them one at a time, until it was as if Look at the fingers of the Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, on his socks."
"1970","(1970) Abd al-Salam bin Harb told us, on the authority of Yazid al-Dalani, on the authority of Yahya bin Ishaq bin Abi Talhi, on the authority of a man From the companions of the Prophet, may God bless him and grant him peace; Concerning a man wiping over his socks, then he appears to take off his socks. He said: He washes his feet."
"1971","(1971) Hushaym told us, on the authority of Zarayya bin Abi Al-Atik, on the authority of Al-Sha’bi, who said: He washes his feet."
"1972","(1972) Hafs told us, on the authority of Sa’id, on the authority of Abu Ma’shar, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: When he wipes and then takes off, he washes his feet."
"1973","(1973) Hafs told us, on the authority of Ash’ath, on the authority of Jahm, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: If someone takes off his socks, he repeats the ablution."
"1974","(1974) Issa bin Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Awza’i, on the authority of Makhoul, and Al-Zuhri. They said: If he wipes and then takes off, they said: Repeats ablution."
"1975","(1975) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Ibrahim; If he takes them off, or one of them, he resumes ablution."
"1976","(1976) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Ibn Sirin, who said: He repeats ablution."
"1977","(1977) Hashim bin Al-Qasim told us, on the authority of Shu’bah, on the authority of Al-Hakam, and Hammad. They said: He performs ablution."
"1978","(1978) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hasan, on the authority of Abd al-Jabbar al-Hamdani, on the authority of al-Sha’abi, who said: If the socks are removed, the wipes are removed."
"1979","(1979) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus and Mansour told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan, that he used to say: When he wiped over He took off his shoes after the event, then he took them off. He was in a state of purity, so let him pray."
"1980","(1980) Hushaym told us, he said: Mughirah and Al-Amash told us, on the authority of Fadl ibn Amr, on the authority of Ibrahim, that He saw Abraham doing that, then he took off his socks and said: Then he prayed but did not perform ablution."
"1981","(1981) Abu Asama told us, on the authority of Ismail, on the authority of Amr bin Dinar, on the authority of Tawus, Concerning a man wiping, then taking off. He said: He used to say: He is on his ritual ablution."
"1982","(1982) Abd al-Samad bin Abd al-Warith narrated to us, on the authority of Sa`id bin Zayd, on the authority of Kathir bin Shindhir, he said: I asked Al-Hasan, And Ata, on the authority of a man who performed ablution and wiped over his socks, then took them off? They said: He prays but does not wash his feet."
"1983","(1983) Ibn Numayr told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Ibrahim, on the authority of Hammam; That Abu Masoud used to wipe over his socks."
"1984","(1984) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Mansour, on the authority of Khalid bin Saad, on the authority of Uqba bin Amr; He wiped over two hair socks."
"1985","(1985) Waki` narrated to us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Abu Qays, on the authority of Dhayl, on the authority of Mughiriya ibn Shu`bah; The Messenger of God, may God bless him and grant him peace, wiped over the socks and sandals. (Tirmidhi 991 Abu Dawud 160)"
"1986","(1986) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Abu Janab, on the authority of his father, on the authority of Jalas bin Amr; Omar performed ablution on Friday, and wiped over his socks and sandals."
"1987","(1987) Abu Bakr bin Ayash told us, on the authority of Husayn, on the authority of Ibrahim, who said: The socks and sandals are in his home. The hidden ones"
"1988","(1988) Hushaym told us, saying: Yunus told us, on the authority of Al-Hasan \n(h) And Shu`bah, on the authority of his leaders, on the authority of Sa`id bin al-Musayyab and al-Hasan, that they said: He wipes over the socks when they are Sfiqin."
"1989","(1989) Hushaym told us, saying: Husayn told us, on the authority of Ibrahim;"
"1990","(1990) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hisham, on the authority of his followers, on the authority of Anas; He was wiping over his socks."
"1991","(1991) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Hammad ibn Salama, on the authority of Abu Ghalib, who said: I saw Abu Imamah wiping over me. The socks."
"1992","(1992) Abu Bakr bin Ayyash told us, on the authority of Abdullah bin Saeed, on the authority of Khalas, who said: I saw Ali urinating, then he wiped over me."
"1993","(1993) Ishaq Al-Azraq told us, on the authority of Juwaybir, on the authority of Al-Dahhak; He used to say about wiping over the socks: There is no problem with it."
"1994","(1994) Ibn Mahdi told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Wasil, on the authority of Saeed bin Abdullah bin Dirar; Anas bin Malik performed ablution and wiped over two socks."
"1995","(1995) Al-Thaqafi told us, on the authority of Ismail bin Umayyah, who said: I have heard that Al-Bara’ bin Aazib did not consider wiping on the The socks are brave.\nAnd I was informed on the authority of Saad bin Abi Waqqas and Saeed bin Al-Musayyab; They did not see any harm in wiping over the socks."
"1996","(1996) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-A’mash, he said: Ismail bin Raji’ told us, on the authority of his father, he said: I saw Al-Bara’a performing ablution. Then he wiped over the socks."
"1997","(1997) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Sufyan, on the authority of Al-Zabarqan Al-Abdi, on the authority of Ka’b bin Abdullah, that Ali urinated, then He performed ablution and wiped over his socks and sandals."
"1998","(1998) Waki’ narrated to us, saying: Zaid bin Mardanabah narrated to us, on the authority of Al-Walid bin Sari’, on the authority of Amr bin Kurayb. Ali performed ablution and wiped over his socks."
"1999","(1999) Waki’ told us, he said: Mahdi bin Maymun told us, on the authority of Wasil Al-Ahdab, on the authority of Abu Wa’il, on the authority of Uqba bin Amr; He performed ablution and wiped over his socks."
"2000","(2000) Waki’ told us, on the authority of Al-Amash, on the authority of Al-Musayyab ibn Rafi’, on the authority of Yasir ibn Amr, who said: I saw Abu Masoud He urinated, then performed ablution and wiped over his socks."
"2001","(2001) Ja’far bin Aoun told us, on the authority of Abu Al-Umays, on the authority of Furat, who said: I saw Sa’id bin Jubayr performing ablution and wiping over me. Socks and slippers."
"2002","(2002) Zayd bin Hubab told us, on the authority of Hisham bin Saad, on the authority of Abu Hazim, on the authority of Sahl bin Saad; He wiped over his socks."
"2003","(2003) Yahya bin Sa’id told us, on the authority of Ibn Jurayj, on the authority of Ata’, who said: Wiping over the socks at home. Wiping over the socks."
"2004","(2004) Abu Dawud told us, on the authority of Abbad bin Rashid, who said: I asked Nafi’ about wiping over socks? He said: They are not as good as the socks."
